window.GUIDE_INDEX=[{"p": "Patient Guide", "t": "What do you need today?", "u": "index.html#browse", "b": "Browse by Topic  Tap a topic. Every page has a quick menu at the top so you can jump straight to what you need. Start Here Why we start with your gut, the toxic bucket, and how habits stick. Read first → Your Program Week-by-week roadmap, your visits, and what comes after graduation. See the roadmap → Daily Habits Hydration, sleep, stress, movement, sun and sweat, in the right order. Build habits → Food & Recipes Meal plan, grocery list, smoothies, treats, and options if you don't cook. Eat well → Natural Remedies Detox bath, teas, companion herbs, binders, and household swaps. Find a remedy →", "k": ""}, {"p": "Patient Guide", "t": "Your gut is your soil.", "u": "index.html#soil", "b": "The Heart of the Bunny Method  A tree is only as healthy as the soil it grows in. Give it rich soil, clean water, sunshine and good neighbors, and it fills with fruit. Your body works the same way. Over your program, you're the gardener. We test the soil, pull the weeds, feed it and water it. Then we watch what grows. Read the Bunny Method → 01 Turn down the drips Fewer toxins in from food, water, products and air. 02 Open the drains Support your liver, gut, kidneys, skin and lungs. 03 Feed the soil Minerals, fiber, good bacteria, sunshine and rest. 04 Track it Energy, sleep, digestion and moo", "k": ""}, {"p": "Patient Guide", "t": "A simple day on the Reset", "u": "index.html#today", "b": "Your Daily Rhythm  Not a rulebook. A rhythm to come back to when the week gets busy. Morning Wake & hydrate A full glass of water with electrolytes and trace minerals. Then 5 to 10 minutes of morning sun outside. Meals Feed the soil Supplements as your label says. Bitters before heavy meals. Plants on most of your plate. Afternoon Move A 20-minute walk keeps your lymph moving. Outside when you can. Evening Wind down No food 2 hours before bed. Dim lights, fewer screens, 7 to 9 hours of sleep.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "Why this guide exists", "u": "start-here.html#welcome", "b": "Welcome  Your body already knows how to heal. Every day it clears out what it doesn't need through your liver, gut, kidneys, lungs and skin. But modern life adds more than our bodies were built to handle. Over months and years, the load builds. That's when you start to feel tired, foggy, bloated, inflamed, or just \"not yourself.\" Your program is about turning that around. We lower the load, open the exits, and rebuild the soil your health grows from. This guide is your companion for every step. How to use this guide Read this page first. It explains the \"why\" behind everything you'll do. Start", "k": ""}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "How to use this guide", "u": "start-here.html#how-to-use", "b": "Read this page first. It explains the \"why\" behind everything you'll do. Start your supplements after your results review, exactly as your label says. Pick one or two habits at a time. Not everything at once. Log how you feel in the Heads Up app . Bring your questions to every visit, so we can talk through what's working.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "This program is a good fit if you're…", "u": "start-here.html#good-fit", "b": "Tired, foggy, bloated, puffy or inflamed Ready to change habits, not just take pills Wanting a strong foundation before hormones or weight-loss medication", "k": ""}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "Always tell us first if you…", "u": "start-here.html#tell-us-first", "b": "Are pregnant, trying to conceive, or breastfeeding Take any daily prescription Have a chronic illness, or kidney or liver disease Have a history of disordered eating Have a surgery or procedure coming up", "k": ""}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "Your gut is your soil", "u": "start-here.html#gut-is-soil", "b": "The Heart of the Bunny Method  Picture a fruit tree. Give it rich soil, clean water, sunshine and good neighbors, and it grows strong. Put the same tree in poor soil and the leaves yellow, the fruit stays small, and pests move in. The tree isn't broken. Its soil is. You are the same. Your gut is where you absorb nutrients, make key vitamins and brain chemicals, and house most of your immune system. When your soil is healthy, you \"bear fruit\": steady energy, clear skin, good sleep, a calm mood. When it isn't, you see the signs: bloating, fatigue, rashes, brain fog and getting sick often. A heal", "k": "soil plant garden microbiome"}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "The toxic bucket", "u": "start-here.html#toxic-bucket", "b": "Toxin Load Over Time  Picture a bucket under a slowly dripping faucet. A few drops a day come from your water, skincare, food, the air and a stressful week. Your body has drains at the bottom: your liver, kidneys, gut, lungs and skin. Problems start when the drips come in faster than the drains let them out, or when a drain gets clogged: a sluggish liver, constipation, poor sleep, chronic stress. The bucket rises slowly, over years. Then one day it overflows. That's when symptoms show up. The good news: your drains respond fast when you support them. food · water · products · air · stress live", "k": "toxins overload bucket"}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "Where toxins sneak in", "u": "start-here.html#where-toxins", "b": "Awareness, Not Fear  You don't need to fear any of these. Just know where the drips come from, so you can turn down the easiest ones first. Source Common examples Food Pesticide residue on conventional produce, processed food additives, seed oils, food dyes Water Chlorine byproducts, PFAS (\"forever chemicals\"), lead from old pipes, fluoride Air Household dust, mold, off-gassing furniture, candles, air fresheners Skin and body products Fragrance, parabens, phthalates in lotion, makeup and hair products Household products Conventional cleaners, dryer sheets, non-stick cookware, plastic food cont", "k": "pfas fragrance plastic pesticides mold"}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "You can change your body", "u": "start-here.html#change-your-body", "b": "Habits and Mindset  Your body is not fixed. Your cells are always renewing. Your gut lining replaces itself every few days. Your gut bacteria shift within days of changing what you eat. Every day, you're building tomorrow's body out of today's choices. 1 Start tiny Make it so easy you can't say no. 2 Stack it Attach a new habit to one you already do. Take your supplements with your morning coffee. 3 Track it What gets tracked gets done. Use the Heads Up app. 4 Expect bumps Missing a day doesn't undo anything. Just restart the next day. Your mindset is part of the protocol How you think about y", "k": "mindset habits motivation"}, {"p": "Start Here", "t": "Your mindset is part of the protocol", "u": "start-here.html#mindset", "b": "How you think about your body shapes how you care for it. If you believe you're healing, every small win counts. Speak to your body like a plant you're helping grow. Patient. Kind. Consistent. Healing isn't a straight line, and every good choice counts. Write it down Three things I want to feel by graduation. Write them in your notes app or journal and read them on hard days. Next: Your Program → Jump to Daily Habits", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Your track is set by your gut", "u": "your-program.html#tracks", "b": "8 or 16 Weeks  Every program runs 16 weeks, with a full recheck at the end. Your Tiny Health gut test score decides how long your intensive Reset phase lasts inside those 16 weeks. Same program, same price, same care. Gut score over 80 8-Week Reset Your soil is in good shape. Your intensive Reset phase runs 8 weeks (2 fast days). Then you move into maintenance habits, plus GLP-1 or hormone therapy if clinically indicated, with the same check-ins and full recheck at week 16 as everyone. Gut score under 80 16-Week Reset Your soil needs more rebuilding. Your Reset phase runs the full 16 weeks, wi", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "What happens, and when", "u": "your-program.html#roadmap", "b": "Your Roadmap  Our front desk books your next step before you leave every visit. All program visits are in person in Fall River. Some follow-ups can be virtual. Getting started Step 1 Website questionnaire A short form so we understand your goals. Our front desk calls you to schedule a phone consultation. Step 2 Intake form Fill it out before your phone consult, so the call is about you, not paperwork. Step 3 Phone consultation We review your history, explain the program, and decide together if it's the right fit. A $200 deposit holds your spot and goes toward your program. Step 4 Blood draw + ", "k": "timeline schedule weeks visits appointments"}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Getting started", "u": "your-program.html#getting-started", "b": "Step 1 Website questionnaire A short form so we understand your goals. Our front desk calls you to schedule a phone consultation. Step 2 Intake form Fill it out before your phone consult, so the call is about you, not paperwork. Step 3 Phone consultation We review your history, explain the program, and decide together if it's the right fit. A $200 deposit holds your spot and goes toward your program. Step 4 Blood draw + live intake Your Bunny Baseline blood work and a 20-minute conversation with your provider. You go home with your Tiny Health gut kit. See blood draw prep . While you wait Star", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Your visits, week by week", "u": "your-program.html#weeks", "b": "The same schedule for both tracks. Week 1 is the week of your results review. Week 1 · In person · 70 min Results review We walk through your labs (20 min) and your gut test (20 min), then build your plan (20 min). Your customized supplement plan and first fast kits start here. Week 3 · Virtual · 20 min Check-in Your supplements are all started by now. We check how you feel and adjust before your first fast day. Week 4 · At home Fast day #1 Your first ProLon fast. See the fast day guide . Week 8 · In person · 30 min Check-in + targeted labs Your mid-point labs: anything that was off on your fi", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Results review", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-1", "b": "Week 1 · In person · 70 min  We walk through your labs (20 min) and your gut test (20 min), then build your plan (20 min). Your customized supplement plan and first fast kits start here.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Check-in", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-3", "b": "Week 3 · Virtual · 20 min  Your supplements are all started by now. We check how you feel and adjust before your first fast day.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Fast day #1", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-4", "b": "Week 4 · At home  Your first ProLon fast. See the fast day guide .", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Check-in + targeted labs", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-8", "b": "Week 8 · In person · 30 min  Your mid-point labs: anything that was off on your first labs, plus hormones, thyroid, vitamin D and B12. If hormone or lean body mass optimization is part of your goals, we look at whether you're ready. 16-week Reset patients pick up their next 8 weeks of supplements and fast kits. 8-week Reset patients graduate from their Reset phase and move into maintenance habits, plus GLP-1 or hormone therapy if clinically indicated.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Check-in + gut retest", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-12", "b": "Week 12 · Virtual · 20 min  We check your progress and send your Tiny Health retest, timed so results are back by graduation.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Full recheck labs", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-15", "b": "Week 15 · In person  Your Bunny Baseline blood work again, so we can compare before and after.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Graduation", "u": "your-program.html#visit-week-16", "b": "Week 16 · In person · 60 min  We compare your labs, gut results and how you feel, and plan your next step. Celebrate.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Between visits", "u": "your-program.html#between-visits", "b": "Weekly check-in text from us through Symplast. Reply with how your week went. Heads Up app every day: symptoms, energy, sleep, digestion, mood and habits. You can track weight here too. Questions anytime: message your provider in the Symplast for Patients app. Don't wait for a visit.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Your tools", "u": "your-program.html#tools", "b": "Included in Your Program  Blood work The Bunny Baseline panel at the start and at graduation, plus add-ons if your results call for them. Tiny Health gut test An at-home gut test at the start and before graduation. It shows, in black and white, how your soil changed. Heads Up app Your wellness hub. Log symptoms and habits, and see your progress. You can track weight here too. Two minutes a day. Symplast for Patients app Your lab reviews, messages with your provider, and appointment details. Download it free on iPhone or Android. Styku body scan A quick 3D scan of body shape, inches and composi", "k": "heads up styku sweatenergy symplast app"}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Blood work", "u": "your-program.html#tool-labs", "b": "The Bunny Baseline panel at the start and at graduation, plus add-ons if your results call for them.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Tiny Health gut test", "u": "your-program.html#tool-gut", "b": "An at-home gut test at the start and before graduation. It shows, in black and white, how your soil changed.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Heads Up app", "u": "your-program.html#tool-headsup", "b": "Your wellness hub. Log symptoms and habits, and see your progress. You can track weight here too. Two minutes a day.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Symplast for Patients app", "u": "your-program.html#tool-symplast", "b": "Your lab reviews, messages with your provider, and appointment details. Download it free on iPhone or Android.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "Styku body scan", "u": "your-program.html#tool-styku", "b": "A quick 3D scan of body shape, inches and composition. It shows changes the scale can miss.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "SweatEnergy", "u": "your-program.html#tool-sweat", "b": "Your included subscription. We activate it with you and show you how to use it. Use it for your workouts: see movement .", "k": ""}, {"p": "Your Program", "t": "After graduation", "u": "your-program.html#after", "b": "What Comes Next  Many patients continue into Hoptimization , our ongoing longevity support. If hormone therapy or weight-loss medication is part of your goals, it's built on top of the foundation you create here. Healthy soil first, then we plant. Hoptimization Continued optimization, labs and support on your own schedule. Lip Bunny Rx Bioidentical hormones (women) and GLP-1 support (women and men) when your labs and symptoms call for it. See Rx patient guides . Why the order matters Every journey starts with the Reset. Medication works best on a balanced foundation. Some patients find they ne", "k": "hoptimization hrt glp-1 core longevity"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Your habit priority list", "u": "daily-habits.html#priority", "b": "Little by Little  We coach one change at a time, in this order. Master one, then add the next. Your provider will tell you which one is your priority right now. 1 Morning Mineral Water A full glass of water with electrolytes and trace minerals when you wake. Then tea or coffee. 2 Electrolytes Minerals so your body holds on to the water you drink. 3 Sleep 7 to 9 hours. Your body does its deepest cleanup at night. 4 Stress Healing runs in \"rest and digest\" mode, not fight-or-flight. 5 Movement Daily walking first, then building muscle. 6 Diet One change at a time. No overhaul required.", "k": "priority order where to start"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Morning mineral water", "u": "daily-habits.html#hydration", "b": "Habit 1  Soil can't grow anything without water, and neither can you. But plain water alone isn't the goal. Too much plain water can dilute your sodium and electrolytes. Try This When You Wake Load your first glass Your lymphatic system works through the night. A big glass of mineral-rich water first thing helps your body flush out what it cleared while you slept. Upon waking: a large, full glass of filtered water. Load it with electrolytes and trace minerals. Easy version: juice of half a lemon and a pinch of sea salt. Then tea or coffee. Coffee tip: waiting 60 to 90 minutes after waking is b", "k": "water hydration lemon sea salt electrolytes trace minerals drink morning coffee lymph"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Load your first glass", "u": "daily-habits.html#lemon-water", "b": "Try This When You Wake  Your lymphatic system works through the night. A big glass of mineral-rich water first thing helps your body flush out what it cleared while you slept. Upon waking: a large, full glass of filtered water. Load it with electrolytes and trace minerals. Easy version: juice of half a lemon and a pinch of sea salt. Then tea or coffee. Coffee tip: waiting 60 to 90 minutes after waking is best. But nobody is perfect.", "k": "lemon water sea salt recipe morning electrolytes trace minerals"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Electrolytes", "u": "daily-habits.html#electrolytes", "b": "Habit 2  Electrolytes (sodium, potassium, magnesium) help your body actually use the water you drink. They matter most on workout days, sauna days, hot days, and fast days. Your morning lemon water with sea salt is your first electrolyte of the day. Add an electrolyte drink around workouts and after sauna or a hot bath. Choose ones without added sugar, artificial sweeteners or dyes. Mineral-rich foods count too: leafy greens, avocado, bananas, nuts and seeds. Check with us first If you have kidney disease, heart failure, or take blood pressure medication or a \"water pill,\" ask before adding sa", "k": "minerals salt potassium magnesium"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Sleep", "u": "daily-habits.html#sleep", "b": "Habit 3  7 to 9 hours nightly. Your brain's \"wash cycle\" runs almost entirely during deep sleep. Skipping sleep is like clogging the drain. Morning and sunset light set your body clock. See your sunlight directions . Your wind-down checklist No food 2 hours before bed Dim the lights after dinner Screens away for the last hour 10 pages of a real book Cool, dark, quiet bedroom Same bedtime most nights, weekends too", "k": "insomnia rest bedtime"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Stress and your nervous system", "u": "daily-habits.html#nervous-system", "b": "Habit 4  Digestion, elimination and repair all run in \"rest and digest\" mode. When you're stuck in fight-or-flight, your body pulls energy away from exactly the pathways this program supports. Calming your nervous system is part of the protocol. Gratitude practice A few minutes of guided gratitude meditation, morning or night. Free guided sessions are easy to find on YouTube. Sound and frequency Calming music or frequency tracks during a bath, a walk or before sleep. Nature Time outside, barefoot on grass or sand, near trees or water. The original reset. Movement and yoga A slow flow or a walk", "k": "stress anxiety calm vagus meditation frequency reiki gratitude"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "The deeper work", "u": "daily-habits.html#deeper-work", "b": "A plant takes on the energy of the place it grows. The people, sounds, words and energy you surround yourself with shape you. Choose an environment you resonate with, and speak kindly to yourself. You're listening too. Connection and purpose Faith, community, real conversations with real people. Connection protects your nervous system. And purpose doesn't need to be grand: being the best parent, friend or caregiver you can be is purpose.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Movement, sun and sweat", "u": "daily-habits.html#movement", "b": "Habit 5  A plant needs sunlight, wind and water moving through it. So do you. Walk daily Even 20 minutes moves your lymph: your body's waste highway, which has no pump except you moving. Walk in nature when you can. Then build muscle Once walking is a habit, add strength work 2 to 3 times a week. Muscle is your metabolism's best friend. Work out with SweatEnergy Your SweatEnergy subscription is included in your program. Use it for your strength workouts at your own pace. We activate it with you. About your tools . Sweat Sauna or a good sweat 2 to 4 times a week, as tolerated, 15 to 20 minutes.", "k": "exercise walk lymph sauna sweat workout muscle"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Walk daily", "u": "daily-habits.html#walking", "b": "Even 20 minutes moves your lymph: your body's waste highway, which has no pump except you moving. Walk in nature when you can.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Then build muscle", "u": "daily-habits.html#muscle", "b": "Once walking is a habit, add strength work 2 to 3 times a week. Muscle is your metabolism's best friend.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Work out with SweatEnergy", "u": "daily-habits.html#sweatenergy", "b": "Your SweatEnergy subscription is included in your program. Use it for your strength workouts at your own pace. We activate it with you. About your tools .", "k": "sweat energy sweatenergy workout exercise app subscription"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Sweat", "u": "daily-habits.html#sweat", "b": "Sauna or a good sweat 2 to 4 times a week, as tolerated, 15 to 20 minutes. Rehydrate with electrolytes afterward. Skip sauna on fast days.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Dry brushing", "u": "daily-habits.html#dry-brushing", "b": "Before a shower, brush skin with gentle strokes toward your heart. Supports skin and lymph flow.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Sunlight, three times a day", "u": "daily-habits.html#sun", "b": "Your Daily Sunshine  Plants run on sunlight. So do you. Light sets your body clock, and a well-set clock supports sleep, mood, hormones and every detox pathway. Morning 5–10 min Go outside and face the sun Let the morning light reach your eyes, as soon as you can after waking. Even 2 minutes is great. Midday 20+ min Direct midday sunlight At least 20 minutes outside in direct sun. A walk at lunch counts. Sunset 5–10 min Watch the sun go down Sunset light tells your body the day is ending, so you're ready to sleep. Even better Go barefoot on grass, sand or soil. Skip sunglasses for these short ", "k": "sun sunlight morning sunset midday outside barefoot grounding vitamin d circadian"}, {"p": "Daily Habits", "t": "Diet, one change at a time", "u": "daily-habits.html#diet-changes", "b": "Habit 6  Food is your biggest lever, but it's last on the list for a reason. Once your hydration, sleep, stress and movement are steady, food changes stick. Add these one at a time: No fast food. Moderate processed sugar and refined carbs. Trade them for a little raw honey or fruit. Your taste buds reset in about two weeks. Moderate alcohol. No food 2 hours before bed. Lemon water with sea salt first thing, every morning. See meals, recipes & grocery list →", "k": "diet food changes sugar alcohol fast food"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Lean into, take a break from", "u": "food.html#lean-into", "b": "The Basics  Eat foods that feed your soil, and take a break from the ones that fill the bucket. This is 80%, not all-or-nothing. Lean into Leafy greens and cruciferous veggies (broccoli, cabbage, brussels sprouts) Beets, artichoke, garlic, onion, lemon Clean protein: wild fish, pasture-raised eggs, organic poultry Healthy fats: olive oil, avocado, nuts, seeds Fiber-rich foods every day Fermented foods: sauerkraut, kimchi, plain yogurt or kefir Fresh herbs at every meal Filtered water through the day Take a break from Alcohol Added sugar and refined carbs Fried foods and seed oils Processed and", "k": "diet eat avoid foods list"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Foods for how you feel", "u": "food.html#foods-for-symptoms", "b": "Food as Medicine  Your plate is your first remedy. Lean into these when a symptom shows up. If it's more than mild or keeps coming back, tell us at your next check-in. Bloating & gas Eat: ginger, fennel, pineapple, papaya, cooked (not raw) veggies, plain yogurt. Eat slowly. Try Better Bitters before heavy meals. Constipation Eat: prunes, kiwi (2 a day), chia and ground flax, pears, berries, leafy greens, lentils. Add fiber slowly. It needs water to work. Low energy Eat: eggs, salmon, lentils, leafy greens, pumpkin seeds, beets, sweet potato, a little dark chocolate. Protein at breakfast keeps ", "k": "symptoms food remedies what to eat"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Bloating & gas", "u": "food.html#food-bloating", "b": "Eat: ginger, fennel, pineapple, papaya, cooked (not raw) veggies, plain yogurt. Eat slowly. Try Better Bitters before heavy meals.", "k": "bloated gas belly digestion"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Constipation", "u": "food.html#food-constipation", "b": "Eat: prunes, kiwi (2 a day), chia and ground flax, pears, berries, leafy greens, lentils. Add fiber slowly. It needs water to work.", "k": "constipated bowel movement regular fiber"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Low energy", "u": "food.html#food-energy", "b": "Eat: eggs, salmon, lentils, leafy greens, pumpkin seeds, beets, sweet potato, a little dark chocolate. Protein at breakfast keeps energy steady all morning.", "k": "tired fatigue energy exhausted"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Brain fog", "u": "food.html#food-brain-fog", "b": "Eat: wild salmon and sardines, walnuts, blueberries, eggs, avocado, fresh rosemary. Brain fog often lifts with steady hydration and less sugar.", "k": "foggy focus memory concentration"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Trouble sleeping", "u": "food.html#food-sleep", "b": "Eat: tart cherries, kiwi, pumpkin seeds, almonds, a banana. Finish eating 2 hours before bed.", "k": "sleep insomnia melatonin"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Stress & anxiety", "u": "food.html#food-stress", "b": "Eat: leafy greens, pumpkin seeds, avocado, dark chocolate, fermented foods like sauerkraut. Magnesium-rich foods help calm the nervous system.", "k": "anxious calm magnesium stress"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Sugar cravings", "u": "food.html#food-cravings", "b": "Eat: protein and healthy fat at every meal, cinnamon, berries, dark chocolate (70%+), chia pudding , energy bites . Cravings drop after about 2 weeks of less sugar.", "k": "sugar sweet craving blood sugar"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Inflammation & aches", "u": "food.html#food-inflammation", "b": "Eat: wild salmon, olive oil, turmeric with black pepper, ginger, berries, cherries, leafy greens. Fried foods, seed oils and sugar are the biggest triggers.", "k": "inflammation joint pain aches sore"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Headaches", "u": "food.html#food-headache", "b": "Eat: bananas, avocado, leafy greens, pumpkin seeds. Most headaches on the program are thirst. See drinks below.", "k": "headache migraine head"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Low mood", "u": "food.html#food-mood", "b": "Eat: fermented foods, salmon, walnuts, eggs, leafy greens, berries, dark chocolate. Your gut makes much of your serotonin. Feed the soil.", "k": "mood sad down depression serotonin"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "PMS & cramps", "u": "food.html#food-pms", "b": "Eat: pumpkin seeds, leafy greens, dark chocolate, salmon, broccoli and cabbage. Cut back on salt, sugar and caffeine the week before your period.", "k": "period cramps pms cycle menstrual"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Hot flashes", "u": "food.html#food-hot-flashes", "b": "Eat: ground flaxseed (1 to 2 tbsp a day), leafy greens, cold-water fish like salmon. Spicy food can be a trigger. Notice yours.", "k": "menopause perimenopause hot flash night sweats"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Getting sick often", "u": "food.html#food-immune", "b": "Eat: garlic, onion, citrus, kiwi, bell peppers, mushrooms, fermented foods. Most of your immune system lives in your gut.", "k": "immune cold flu sick zinc vitamin c"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Nausea", "u": "food.html#food-nausea", "b": "Eat: ginger chews, plain crackers, banana, rice, small bland meals. Small amounts, often. Stop before you feel full.", "k": "nausea queasy sick stomach"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Drinks for how you feel", "u": "food.html#drinks-for-symptoms", "b": "Sip Your Medicine  Teas, waters, broths and smoothies to reach for. Tap a smoothie name for its recipe. Bloating & gas Sip: hibiscus tea, fennel tea, ginger tea. Sip warm drinks between meals, not with them. Constipation Sip: warm lemon water first thing, plenty of water all day, a small glass of prune juice. Fiber without water can make it worse. Low energy Sip: your morning mineral water first, then green tea or matcha, coconut water, a Beet and Berry smoothie . Afternoon slump? Try water with sea salt before a second coffee. Brain fog Sip: mineral water through the day, green tea or matcha,", "k": "drinks tea symptoms what to drink"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Bloating & gas", "u": "food.html#drink-bloating", "b": "Sip: hibiscus tea, fennel tea, ginger tea. Sip warm drinks between meals, not with them.", "k": "bloated gas tea hibiscus fennel"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Constipation", "u": "food.html#drink-constipation", "b": "Sip: warm lemon water first thing, plenty of water all day, a small glass of prune juice. Fiber without water can make it worse.", "k": "constipated water prune juice"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Low energy", "u": "food.html#drink-energy", "b": "Sip: your morning mineral water first, then green tea or matcha, coconut water, a Beet and Berry smoothie . Afternoon slump? Try water with sea salt before a second coffee.", "k": "tired energy matcha green tea"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Brain fog", "u": "food.html#drink-brain-fog", "b": "Sip: mineral water through the day, green tea or matcha, a Bunny Green smoothie . Even mild dehydration can blur focus.", "k": "foggy focus green tea"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Trouble sleeping", "u": "food.html#drink-sleep", "b": "Sip: chamomile tea, a small glass of unsweetened tart cherry juice, warm golden milk. No caffeine after noon.", "k": "sleep chamomile tart cherry golden milk"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Stress & anxiety", "u": "food.html#drink-stress", "b": "Sip: chamomile, lemon balm or holy basil (tulsi) tea. Swap the second coffee for a calming tea.", "k": "anxious calm tea tulsi lemon balm"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Sugar cravings", "u": "food.html#drink-cravings", "b": "Sip: filtered water with lemon or berries, cinnamon tea, a Creamy Cacao smoothie . Thirst often feels like a craving. Drink first.", "k": "sugar craving soda water"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Inflammation & aches", "u": "food.html#drink-inflammation", "b": "Sip: ginger tea, green tea, bone broth, a Golden Turmeric smoothie . Skip soda, energy drinks and alcohol.", "k": "inflammation turmeric ginger broth"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Headaches", "u": "food.html#drink-headache", "b": "Sip: water with a pinch of sea salt or electrolytes, coconut water, ginger tea. Hydrate first. Most headaches on the program are thirst.", "k": "headache water electrolytes"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Low mood", "u": "food.html#drink-mood", "b": "Sip: kefir, warm unsweetened cacao, a Bunny Green smoothie . Alcohol lowers mood the next day. Take a break from it.", "k": "mood kefir cacao"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "PMS & cramps", "u": "food.html#drink-pms", "b": "Sip: ginger tea, chamomile tea, warm unsweetened cacao. A warm drink and a heating pad go a long way.", "k": "period cramps tea"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Hot flashes", "u": "food.html#drink-hot-flashes", "b": "Sip: cool water through the day, sage tea. Alcohol, caffeine and very hot drinks can trigger flashes.", "k": "menopause hot flash sage tea water"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Getting sick often", "u": "food.html#drink-immune", "b": "Sip: bone broth, ginger-lemon-honey tea, plenty of warm fluids. Rest and fluids first when you feel something coming on.", "k": "immune cold flu broth tea"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Nausea", "u": "food.html#drink-nausea", "b": "Sip: ginger tea, small sips of broth or electrolytes. Sip slowly and often. Call us if you can't keep fluids down.", "k": "nausea ginger"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Food for beauty", "u": "food.html#beauty-foods", "b": "Beauty From the Inside Out  Healthy soil grows beautiful fruit. Your skin, hair and nails show what's happening inside. Feed them here. Glowing skin Reach for: water with minerals, avocado, olive oil, salmon, walnuts, colorful veggies (carrots, sweet potato, peppers). Healthy fats keep skin soft and hydrated from the inside. Collagen & firmness Reach for: bone broth, eggs, chicken, fish, plus vitamin C foods (citrus, kiwi, strawberries, bell peppers). Your body needs vitamin C to build collagen. Pair them. Clearer skin Reach for: pumpkin seeds (zinc), leafy greens, berries, fermented foods, pl", "k": "beauty skin hair nails glow food"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Glowing skin", "u": "food.html#beauty-glow", "b": "Reach for: water with minerals, avocado, olive oil, salmon, walnuts, colorful veggies (carrots, sweet potato, peppers). Healthy fats keep skin soft and hydrated from the inside.", "k": "skin glow dry dull"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Collagen & firmness", "u": "food.html#beauty-collagen", "b": "Reach for: bone broth, eggs, chicken, fish, plus vitamin C foods (citrus, kiwi, strawberries, bell peppers). Your body needs vitamin C to build collagen. Pair them.", "k": "collagen firm wrinkles aging"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Clearer skin", "u": "food.html#beauty-acne", "b": "Reach for: pumpkin seeds (zinc), leafy greens, berries, fermented foods, plenty of fiber. Sugar and, for some people, dairy can trigger breakouts. Track it.", "k": "acne breakouts pimples clear skin"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Stronger hair", "u": "food.html#beauty-hair", "b": "Reach for: eggs, salmon, lentils, beef or chicken, pumpkin seeds, spinach, sweet potato. Hair needs protein and iron. Low iron is a common cause of shedding. We check it on your labs.", "k": "hair loss shedding thinning growth"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Healthy nails", "u": "food.html#beauty-nails", "b": "Reach for: eggs, almonds, salmon, lentils, leafy greens. Brittle nails can point to low protein or iron.", "k": "nails brittle"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Less puffiness", "u": "food.html#beauty-puffiness", "b": "Reach for: cucumber, watermelon, celery, bananas, avocado, leafy greens. Less processed salty food. Potassium-rich foods help balance salt. Lemon water helps too.", "k": "puffy bags under eye swelling water retention"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Sun support from within", "u": "food.html#beauty-sun", "b": "Reach for: cooked tomatoes and tomato sauce, carrots, sweet potato, watermelon, green tea, olive oil. Carotenoid-rich foods may support skin, but they never replace sunscreen.", "k": "sun protection lycopene carotenoid"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Aging gracefully", "u": "food.html#beauty-aging", "b": "Reach for: berries, green tea, dark chocolate, leafy greens, olive oil, cruciferous veggies, fresh herbs. Antioxidant-rich plants at every meal. Color is the clue.", "k": "anti aging antioxidants longevity"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "A bonus for skin & thyroid", "u": "food.html#beauty-selenium", "b": "Reach for: Brazil nuts: just 1 to 2 a day for selenium. More is not better. Too much selenium can cause problems.", "k": "brazil nuts selenium thyroid"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "The Dirty Dozen & Clean Fifteen", "u": "food.html#dirty-dozen", "b": "Shop Smart  You don't need to buy everything organic. Just the produce that carries the most pesticide residue. Frozen organic counts and is usually cheaper. Lists are updated yearly by the Environmental Working Group (EWG). Dirty Dozen: buy organic Strawberries · Spinach · Kale, collard and mustard greens · Grapes · Peaches · Pears · Nectarines · Apples · Bell and hot peppers · Cherries · Blueberries · Green beans Clean Fifteen: conventional is fine Avocados · Sweet corn · Pineapple · Onions · Papaya · Sweet peas (frozen) · Asparagus · Cabbage · Watermelon · Mushrooms · Mango · Sweet potatoes", "k": "organic pesticides dirty dozen clean fifteen produce"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "2-week meal plan", "u": "food.html#meal-plan", "b": "A Template, Not a Rulebook  Tap any meal to open its recipe. Swap meals, repeat favorites, and rotate these two weeks for your whole program. Week 1 Day Breakfast Lunch Dinner Snack 1 Veggie scramble, spinach and avocado Grilled chicken salad, lemon-olive oil dressing Baked salmon, roasted broccoli, quinoa Apple + almonds 2 Chia pudding with berries Turkey lettuce wraps, veggies Chicken or tofu stir-fry, mixed veggies, rice Carrots + hummus 3 Bunny Green smoothie Lentil soup + side salad Shrimp tacos, corn tortillas, cabbage slaw with cilantro Cucumber + guacamole 4 Eggs, sautéed greens, sweet", "k": "meals menu breakfast lunch dinner snack plan"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Week 1", "u": "food.html#meal-week-1", "b": "Day Breakfast Lunch Dinner Snack 1 Veggie scramble, spinach and avocado Grilled chicken salad, lemon-olive oil dressing Baked salmon, roasted broccoli, quinoa Apple + almonds 2 Chia pudding with berries Turkey lettuce wraps, veggies Chicken or tofu stir-fry, mixed veggies, rice Carrots + hummus 3 Bunny Green smoothie Lentil soup + side salad Shrimp tacos, corn tortillas, cabbage slaw with cilantro Cucumber + guacamole 4 Eggs, sautéed greens, sweet potato hash Quinoa bowl, roasted veggies, chickpeas, parsley Herb-roasted chicken thighs, asparagus, wild rice Walnuts + orange 5 Bunny Overnight Ch", "k": ""}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Week 2", "u": "food.html#meal-week-2", "b": "Day Breakfast Lunch Dinner Snack 8 Smoothie bowl, hemp seeds and granola Salmon salad, mixed greens Chicken fajita bowl, peppers, onions, rice, cilantro Orange + walnuts 9 Chia pudding, mango Turkey and veggie soup Baked cod, roasted cabbage, wild rice Cucumber + hummus 10 Veggie scramble, side of berries Big salad, grilled shrimp Herb chicken, roasted carrots, quinoa Celery + almond butter 11 Bunny Overnight Chia Lentil and veggie bowl Turkey burger, lettuce wrap, side salad Apple + almonds 12 Bunny Green smoothie Leftover turkey burger bowl Baked salmon, asparagus, sweet potato Berries + coc", "k": ""}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Grocery list", "u": "food.html#grocery-list", "b": "Print or Screenshot  Produce Spinach and leafy greens Broccoli, cabbage, brussels sprouts Avocados Sweet potatoes, carrots Cucumber, celery Lemons, berries, apples Garlic, onion, ginger Fresh parsley, cilantro, basil, oregano, thyme, rosemary Protein Wild salmon and cod Shrimp Organic chicken thighs Ground turkey Pasture-raised eggs Tofu (optional) Chickpeas and lentils Pantry & other Quinoa, wild rice Ancient grains (buckwheat, spelt, einkorn) Real sourdough from a local bakery Refrigerated sauerkraut or kimchi Olive oil Almonds, walnuts, chia seeds, pumpkin seeds Almond butter, hummus Coconu", "k": "shopping list groceries"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Smoothies", "u": "food.html#smoothies", "b": "Blend, Sip, Done  Tap a smoothie for the full recipe. Add a scoop of collagen or clean protein powder to turn any of these into a full meal. Liver support Bunny Green Spinach, cucumber, green apple, lemon juice, a small handful of parsley, filtered water. Antioxidants Berry Antioxidant Mixed berries, coconut yogurt, chia seeds, almond milk. Digestion Tropical Gut Reset Pineapple, mango, ginger, coconut water, fresh mint. Energy Creamy Cacao Banana, cacao powder, almond butter, almond milk, cinnamon. Circulation Beet and Berry Cooked beet, blueberries, banana, almond milk, fresh ginger. Inflamm", "k": "smoothie recipes bunny green"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Sweet treats", "u": "food.html#treats", "b": "Yes, You Can Have Dessert  Tap a treat for the recipe. Dark chocolate + sea salt 1 to 2 squares, 70%+ cacao. Energy bites Dates, almond butter, chia seeds and cinnamon, rolled and chilled. Frozen banana bites Banana slices dipped in dark chocolate, then frozen. Baked cinnamon apples Sliced apple, cinnamon and a drizzle of honey. Chia pudding cups Chia, almond milk, vanilla and berries. Berries + coconut whip Simple, fresh, done.", "k": "dessert sugar cravings sweets chocolate"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Picky eaters", "u": "food.html#picky-eaters", "b": "Veggie Haters Welcome  If the taste or texture of vegetables is a dealbreaker, forcing it isn't the answer. There are real ways to close the gap. Disguise tricks that work Blend spinach or zucchini into marinara, chili or fruit smoothies Stir riced cauliflower or broccoli into regular rice Swap pasta for zucchini or hearts of palm noodles in a sauce you love Grate carrot or zucchini into muffins or banana bread Greens powders Tier Pick Why High-end AG1 80+ ingredients. Earthy taste. Priciest. Mid Bloom Greens or Supergreen Tonik Easier flavor, about half the cost Basic Amazing Grass or Live it", "k": "hate vegetables greens powder picky"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Disguise tricks that work", "u": "food.html#disguise", "b": "Blend spinach or zucchini into marinara, chili or fruit smoothies Stir riced cauliflower or broccoli into regular rice Swap pasta for zucchini or hearts of palm noodles in a sauce you love Grate carrot or zucchini into muffins or banana bread", "k": ""}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Greens powders", "u": "food.html#greens-powders", "b": "Tier Pick Why High-end AG1 80+ ingredients. Earthy taste. Priciest. Mid Bloom Greens or Supergreen Tonik Easier flavor, about half the cost Basic Amazing Grass or Live it Up Budget-friendly, organic, simple Eating vegetables a real struggle? Bring it up at a check-in. We'll find a way that works for you.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Don't cook? Here's your plan", "u": "food.html#no-cook", "b": "Busy? No Problem.  Meal delivery Tier Pick Why High-end CookUnity Chef-made dishes that rotate weekly Mid Factor Reliable, heats in 2 to 3 minutes Basic Clean Eatz Kitchen Frozen, no subscription The no-prep grocery run Any protein plus any produce below is a real meal in under 10 minutes. Protein, cooked Wild canned salmon or sardines · Pre-cooked shrimp · Hard-boiled eggs · Pre-cooked meatballs · Plain Greek yogurt or cottage cheese · Canned beans or lentils Produce, done Salad kits · Steam-in-bag veggies · Pre-cut fruit · Frozen riced cauliflower · Frozen edamame · Roasted chickpeas", "k": "meal delivery no cooking busy quick"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "The no-prep grocery run", "u": "food.html#no-prep", "b": "Any protein plus any produce below is a real meal in under 10 minutes. Protein, cooked Wild canned salmon or sardines · Pre-cooked shrimp · Hard-boiled eggs · Pre-cooked meatballs · Plain Greek yogurt or cottage cheese · Canned beans or lentils Produce, done Salad kits · Steam-in-bag veggies · Pre-cut fruit · Frozen riced cauliflower · Frozen edamame · Roasted chickpeas", "k": ""}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Alkaline vs. acid-forming foods", "u": "food.html#alkaline", "b": "Balance Your Plate  Like soil, your body does best with the right pH. Your body controls your blood pH tightly on its own, but your daily food choices shape the load it has to balance. You don't need to eat 100% alkaline. Just tip most meals toward the first column. Category Alkaline-forming (favor) Acid-forming (limit) Greens Spinach, kale, chard, arugula, collards, romaine, broccoli, cauliflower, brussels sprouts, cabbage Other vegetables Cucumber, celery, carrots, beets, zucchini, sweet potato, asparagus, peppers, onion, garlic, mushrooms Fruits Lemon and lime, avocado, watermelon, cantalou", "k": "ph acid alkaline foods chart"}, {"p": "Food & Recipes", "t": "Intermittent fasting, day to day", "u": "food.html#intermittent-fasting", "b": "Daily Rhythm  Between your ProLon fast days, a daily eating window gives your gut a longer rest each night. Style Eating window Good starting point if… 12:12 12 hours You're new to fasting. Basically, no snacking after dinner. 14:10 10 hours 12:12 feels easy and you want a gentle next step 16:8 8 hours You want a more established routine Check with us first Start with 12:12 for at least a week before tightening. Black coffee, plain tea and water don't break a fast. If you feel dizzy, shaky or unwell, eat. Ask us first if you take blood sugar medication, are pregnant or breastfeeding, or have a", "k": "intermittent fasting 12:12 16:8 eating window"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Quick help by symptom", "u": "remedies.html#quick-help", "b": "Feeling Off?  Gentle things to try at home. If a symptom is more than mild, lasts more than a few days, or worries you, message us or call (508) 388-2200 . For what to eat, see foods for how you feel . Constipation or no daily bowel movement Daily bowel movements are a must during your Reset. Waste that sits too long can be reabsorbed. Lemon water with sea salt first thing, then more water through the day Take your fiber with a full glass of water Walk after meals Magnesium in the evening, as your label says 2 prunes or dates a day Reach out No bowel movement for 2+ days, or belly pain, vomiti", "k": "symptoms help relief"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Constipation or no daily bowel movement", "u": "remedies.html#constipation", "b": "Daily bowel movements are a must during your Reset. Waste that sits too long can be reabsorbed. Lemon water with sea salt first thing, then more water through the day Take your fiber with a full glass of water Walk after meals Magnesium in the evening, as your label says 2 prunes or dates a day Reach out No bowel movement for 2+ days, or belly pain, vomiting or fever.", "k": "constipated no bowel movement poop stool"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Bloating or gas", "u": "remedies.html#bloating", "b": "Better Bitters spray 10 to 15 minutes before heavy meals (meat, dairy, foods that bloat you) Hibiscus or ginger lemon tea after meals Eat slowly and chew well. Stop at 80% full. Introduce fiber slowly and drink more water with it A short walk after eating Bloating can happen in the first weeks of new gut support. Tell us at your check-in if it isn't settling.", "k": "bloated gas belly"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Headache, tiredness or feeling \"off\" when starting something new", "u": "remedies.html#headache", "b": "What's normal: in the first few days of a new step, you may feel a little more tired or foggy, a mild headache or achiness, a mild \"flu-like\" feeling, or changes in digestion. Your body is doing real work. Hydrate: lemon water with sea salt, plus electrolytes Make sure you're having a daily bowel movement A detox bath and an early night Walk gently. Skip hard workouts. Reach out Reactions more than mild, lasting more than a few days, a new rash or hives, belly pain, vomiting or fever.", "k": "head pain tired foggy flu-like reaction die-off"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Nausea", "u": "remedies.html#nausea", "b": "Ginger lemon tea, or a ginger supplement Smaller meals, eaten slowly. Stop before you feel full. Avoid greasy, fried and very sweet foods Sip fluids between meals rather than with them On a GLP-1? See GLP-1 side effect support . Call us if you can't keep fluids down.", "k": "nausea sick stomach queasy"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Trouble sleeping", "u": "remedies.html#poor-sleep", "b": "Magnesium in the evening, as your label says A warm detox bath an hour before bed No food 2 hours before bed, no screens the last hour Morning sunlight to set your body clock Calming music or a frequency track as you fall asleep Tell us if a new supplement seems to make you wired or anxious. Some B vitamins can, and we can adjust.", "k": "insomnia cant sleep restless"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Stressed or overwhelmed", "u": "remedies.html#stress-day", "b": "Slow breathing: in for 4, out for 6, for 3 minutes Get outside. Barefoot on grass if you can. A gratitude meditation, morning or night Pick one habit this week, not five See the nervous system connection for more tools.", "k": "anxious overwhelmed stressed"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "The Bunny Bath", "u": "remedies.html#detox-bath", "b": "Ritual  A warm bath supports your skin, your largest exit route, and helps you wind down. Recipe Add to a warm bath 2 cups Epsom salt 2 cups sea salt 1 cup baking soda Soak 20 minutes. Rinse off, rehydrate with water and electrolytes, and moisturize with a clean lotion or oil. Why it works Epsom salt (magnesium) relaxes muscles and calms the nervous system. Sea salt adds minerals. Baking soda softens and soothes skin. Make it a ritual Dim the lights, put on calming music or a frequency track, and leave your phone in another room. Skip or ask first Skip hot baths if you're pregnant. Check with ", "k": "epsom salt bath soak baking soda"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Teas & tonics", "u": "remedies.html#teas", "b": "Warm Cups  Warm drinks support digestion and hydration, and give you something soothing to reach for instead of a second coffee. Dandelion root Traditionally used for liver and bile flow. One cup daily. Skip if you have kidney disease. Milk thistle Gentle liver support. One cup daily. Ginger lemon Warming. Great after meals and for nausea. Hibiscus Tart, antioxidant-rich and caffeine-free. Hot or iced. Great on your fast day. Skip if pregnant. Ask us first if you take blood pressure or diabetes medication. Wellness Hunny Chai Simmer 2 cups water with 1 Earl Grey or black tea bag and a pinch ea", "k": "tea chai wellness hunny earl grey black tea dandelion milk thistle hibiscus ginger"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Wellness Hunny Chai", "u": "remedies.html#bunny-chai", "b": "Simmer 2 cups water with 1 Earl Grey or black tea bag and a pinch each of cloves, Ceylon cinnamon, nutmeg, cardamom, a little cayenne, fresh ginger, turmeric and a crack of black pepper for 10 minutes. Strain, add warm milk of choice, and sweeten with maple syrup or honey to taste. The black pepper helps you absorb the turmeric. Use decaf tea in the evening or on fast days.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Companion herbs for your soil", "u": "remedies.html#herbs", "b": "Good Neighbors  Gardeners have planted herbs next to crops for centuries to keep pests away. Many of those same herbs help keep your inner garden in balance. A small handful at one meal a day is the whole habit. Herb In the garden For you Easy ways to use it Oregano Planted to repel pests Contains carvacrol, a natural antimicrobial Sauces, eggs, roasted veggies, dressing Thyme Protects nearby plants Contains thymol. Traditionally used for immune and respiratory support. Soups, roasted chicken and veggies Basil The classic tomato companion Antioxidant, with a calming effect Salads, pesto, smoot", "k": "oregano thyme basil parsley cilantro rosemary wormwood herbs"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Binders", "u": "remedies.html#binders", "b": "What Escorts Waste Out  Once your liver and gut release waste, something needs to grab it in the gut so it leaves in your stool instead of being reabsorbed. That's the job of a binder. Your everyday binder Your GLP-1 Daily Support Fiber binds waste, feeds your good bacteria and keeps you regular. It's often part of your supplement plan. Stronger binders, only when we prescribe them Binder When we use it Modified citrus pectin (like PectaClear) Spike protein and heavy metal add-on protocols Activated charcoal Occasionally, for a rough day (headache, fatigue) Zeolite Regular (non-nano) zeolite o", "k": "binder charcoal zeolite pectin fiber"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Stronger binders, only when we prescribe them", "u": "remedies.html#stronger-binders", "b": "Binder When we use it Modified citrus pectin (like PectaClear) Spike protein and heavy metal add-on protocols Activated charcoal Occasionally, for a rough day (headache, fatigue) Zeolite Regular (non-nano) zeolite only. Nano particles are small enough to cross the gut lining. Timing rule Keep binders at least 2 hours away from food, medications and other supplements. Binders can grab those too.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Your pH tracking", "u": "remedies.html#ph", "b": "A Daily Mirror  Your urine pH is a simple daily mirror of how your food and habits are balancing out. Use the pH strips in your welcome bag on your first-morning urine . Healthy range First-morning urine is generally 6.5 to 7.5 . Don't stress over one reading. Look at the weekly trend. Why terrain matters Unwanted organisms tend to thrive in an acidic, low-oxygen environment, like weeds in poor soil. Alkaline foods and herbs help change the terrain. Log your readings in Heads Up .", "k": "ph strips urine test alkaline"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Water filtration, budget to premium", "u": "remedies.html#water-filters", "b": "Clean Water  Any filter is better than none. Look for the NSF certification number on the box. That's the difference between marketing and a lab-verified claim. Budget Brita Elite pitcher NSF-certified for chlorine and lead. Swap filters about every 6 months. Better Clearly Filtered pitcher Lead, PFAS (\"forever chemicals\") and chlorine. Premium AquaTru countertop RO PFAS, lead, fluoride and more. No plumbing needed. Whole home Under-sink or whole-house RO Every tap filtered. Get a quote from a local installer.", "k": "filter brita aquatru reverse osmosis pfas"}, {"p": "Natural Remedies", "t": "Household & product swaps", "u": "remedies.html#swaps", "b": "Pulling Weeds, One at a Time  Swap products out as they run out. No need to throw everything away today. Category Swap to What to look for All-purpose cleaner Plant-based or DIY cleaner Fragrance-free. No bleach or ammonia. DIY: white vinegar and water for glass, baking soda for scrubbing. Laundry Fragrance-free detergent No added fragrance or optical brighteners. Wool dryer balls instead of dryer sheets. Dish soap Fragrance-free dish soap Short ingredient list. No added dyes or fragrance. Toothpaste Cleaner toothpaste No artificial dyes or sweeteners. Ask us about fluoride vs. hydroxyapatite ", "k": "clean products cleaner toothpaste deodorant makeup cookware laundry fragrance plastic"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Your customized supplement plan", "u": "supplements.html#core-5", "b": "Built for You  Your plan is built from your labs, your gut test and your symptoms. These are the foundation supplements most plans include. Each one supports a part of your \"soil.\" They start after your results review , not before. Always follow the dose on your label. Your provider may adjust it for you. 1 Methyl Protect When: morning, after breakfast. Active B vitamins (folate, B12, B6) that power your liver's detox steps, energy and mood. Tell us if you feel wired, anxious, irritable or can't sleep after starting. We can adjust. 2 Vitamin D3 + K When: after a meal with healthy fats. Your \"s", "k": "customized supplement plan core five supplements methyl protect vitamin d magnesium fiber bitters"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Methyl Protect", "u": "supplements.html#methyl-protect", "b": "1  When: morning, after breakfast. Active B vitamins (folate, B12, B6) that power your liver's detox steps, energy and mood. Tell us if you feel wired, anxious, irritable or can't sleep after starting. We can adjust.", "k": "b vitamins folate b12 methylation"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Vitamin D3 + K", "u": "supplements.html#vitamin-d", "b": "2  When: after a meal with healthy fats. Your \"sunshine\" nutrient for immune system, mood, bones and hormones. Vitamin K helps send calcium to your bones. Tell us if you take a blood thinner like warfarin. Vitamin K can interact.", "k": "vitamin d3 k2 sunshine"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Magnesium Glycinate", "u": "supplements.html#magnesium", "b": "3  When: evening or bedtime. A key mineral for your \"soil pH.\" Calms the nervous system, supports sleep and regularity, and activates vitamin D. Loose stools? Take fewer capsules and build up slowly.", "k": "magnesium glycinate sleep calm"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "GLP-1 Daily Support Fiber", "u": "supplements.html#fiber", "b": "4  When: one scoop in water, before a meal. Feeds your good gut bacteria, keeps you regular, carries waste out, and supports steady blood sugar and fullness. Start slow and drink a full glass of water with it.", "k": "glp-1 fiber powder binder regular"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Better Bitters", "u": "supplements.html#better-bitters", "b": "5  When: 10 to 15 minutes before heavy meals (meat, dairy, foods that bloat you), 1 to 2 times a day. A plant-based spray that wakes up stomach acid and bile so you digest heavier meals better. Contains alcohol. Tell us if you avoid alcohol, have ulcers, reflux or gallstones.", "k": "bitters digestion bloating spray"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Supplement library", "u": "supplements.html#library", "b": "Our Dispensary  Every supplement we carry. Tap one to see what it does, the ingredients, dietary info, certifications, the best time of day to take it and tips. Your plan tells you which ones are yours. About this information Compiled from Fullscript and brand listings, November 2026. Every brand on Fullscript must show proof of third-party cGMP certification each year. Formulas can change, so always check your bottle. None of these products list kosher certification on Fullscript; if you keep kosher, ask us and we'll check your specific bottles.", "k": "supplement library list vegan kosher gluten free ingredients certifications"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Supplement rules", "u": "supplements.html#rules", "b": "Keep It Safe  1 Your label is the boss Your dose and timing are on your label and your plan. Follow those over anything general you read here or online. 2 One new thing at a time Start one new supplement every couple of days, unless we tell you otherwise. If something doesn't agree with you, you'll know which one. 3 Fiber and binders: 2 hours from meds Take fiber and binders at least 2 hours away from prescriptions, including thyroid medication and birth control, so they don't block absorption. 4 Tell us about every medication Including new prescriptions, over-the-counter meds and herbs. Some ", "k": "timing medications safety rules interactions"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Personalized gut support", "u": "supplements.html#gut-support", "b": "Built From Your Gut Test  Your Tiny Health gut test shows which bacteria live in your gut and what they're doing. No two results look the same, so no two gut plans are the same. We match food first, then targeted supplements, to what your results show. 1 Food first Most gut results improve with the right foods. Your plan always starts here. 2 Targeted support Probiotics, fibers or other gut supplements only when your results call for them. 3 Retest Your gut retest near the end of your program shows how your soil changed. What your results might show, and how we support it Your results show Foo", "k": "gut test results probiotic prebiotic butyrate histamine estrogen sbo kit antimicrobial personalized gut supplements tiny health"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "What your results might show, and how we support it", "u": "supplements.html#gut-results-guide", "b": "Your results show Food support Supplements we may add Low diversity or one type taking over A wide variety of plants each week, fermented foods, time in nature and around animals Usually food is enough Low butyrate (fuel for your gut lining) Resistant starch and inulin: beans, lentils, soups and stews, cooked-then-cooled potatoes and rice, onions, garlic A prebiotic fiber, or a probiotic with butyrate-producing strains Thin gut lining (mucus-eating bacteria are high) Polyphenol-rich foods: berries, green tea, olive oil, colorful produce Gut-lining support such as serum bovine immunoglobulins (", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Antimicrobial kits (like the SBO kit)", "u": "supplements.html#gut-reset-kit", "b": "Case by case only  Strong herbal antimicrobials, like oregano oil and wormwood, don't only target the bad bacteria. They can also knock back the good ones. So we don't give them to everyone. If your results show a real overgrowth, we choose the gentlest option that will work, often a garlic-based extract first. Stronger kits are reserved for specific cases, at the lowest dose and shortest time that does the job. Not for pregnancy, trying to conceive or breastfeeding. A few days of feeling tired, achy or bloated can happen. Tell us if it's more than mild.", "k": "sbo kit antimicrobial wormwood oregano overgrowth"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Good to know", "u": "supplements.html#probiotic-tips", "b": "Not all probiotics are equal. We pick strains that fit your results. Some can add to histamine or bloating. Pause probiotics 3 to 5 days before any gut test. Some gut supplements can slow your bowels. Tell us if you get constipated. Your gut results show patterns and connections, not diagnoses. We read them alongside your labs and symptoms. Tell us about every supplement you already take. More is not better for your gut.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Add-ons we may recommend", "u": "supplements.html#add-ons", "b": "Only If Recommended for You  Your labs and symptoms may point to extra support. These are only added if your provider recommends them, and they're priced separately. Ask at any check-in if you're curious. Spike Protein Support For an elevated spike protein antibody level plus symptoms like fatigue or brain fog. Low Iron Support For low ferritin (iron stores) on your labs. Heavy Metal Support When your history or labs point to a heavy metal burden. Symptom Support Extra help for digestion, sleep, stress, hormones or heart health, based on your labs.", "k": "spike protein iron heavy metals add on extra"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Refills & ordering", "u": "supplements.html#refills", "b": "Running Low?  During your program Your supplements and ProLon kits are given to you in 8-week supplies. On the 16-week Reset, you pick up your second supply at your week 8 visit. After your program Keep going with the same supplements. Two easy ways: Pick them up at Lip Bunny. We keep most supplements in stock. Call or message us so it's ready when you come in. Order online through our Fullscript dispensary, shipped to your door. Open Fullscript → Not sure what to reorder? Message us in the Symplast for Patients app before you buy.", "k": "order reorder fullscript refill buy"}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Supplement questions", "u": "supplements.html#supplement-faq", "b": "Common Questions  I forgot my supplements. Should I double up? No. Just take your next dose at the usual time. Missing a day doesn't undo anything. Do I take supplements on my fast day? No. Pause all your supplements on your ProLon fast day and restart with breakfast the next morning. Keep taking prescription medications unless we told you otherwise. Can I keep taking my own supplements? Bring everything you take to your results review. Some may overlap with your plan, and some may interact. We'll tell you what to keep, pause or stop. A supplement is upsetting my stomach. Try taking it with fo", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "I forgot my supplements. Should I double up?", "u": "supplements.html#missed-supplement", "b": "No. Just take your next dose at the usual time. Missing a day doesn't undo anything.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Do I take supplements on my fast day?", "u": "supplements.html#supplements-fast-day", "b": "No. Pause all your supplements on your ProLon fast day and restart with breakfast the next morning. Keep taking prescription medications unless we told you otherwise.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "Can I keep taking my own supplements?", "u": "supplements.html#own-supplements", "b": "Bring everything you take to your results review. Some may overlap with your plan, and some may interact. We'll tell you what to keep, pause or stop.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "A supplement is upsetting my stomach.", "u": "supplements.html#supplement-upset", "b": "Try taking it with food (unless the label says empty stomach). If it doesn't settle in a few days, pause that one supplement and message us.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Supplements", "t": "I have trouble swallowing pills.", "u": "supplements.html#pill-trouble", "b": "Let us know. Many supplements come as powders, liquids or smaller capsules, and some capsules can be opened into food. Ask before opening any capsule.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Your day at a glance", "u": "fast-days.html#your-day", "b": "Meal What's in your kit Breakfast Nut-based bar, herbal tea, algal oil Lunch ProLon soup, crackers, NR-1 packets Afternoon Olives, herbal tea Dinner ProLon soup, Choco Crisp bar Follow the meal plan printed on your box. Contents can vary slightly by kit version.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Your fast schedule", "u": "fast-days.html#schedule", "b": "Mark Your Calendar  One fast day every 4 weeks, starting after your results review. We'll help you pick the dates. Put them in your phone calendar today. 8-Week Reset 2 fast days Week 4 Fast #1 Your first fast. Keep the day calm. Week 8 Fast #2 Your body knows the drill now. 16-Week Reset 3 fast days Week 4 Fast #1 Your first fast. Keep the day calm. Week 8 Fast #2 Pick up your next kits at your week 8 visit. Week 12 Fast #3 Your last program fast. Default fast day is Wednesday. Ask us if Sunday works better. Missed one? Message us and we'll pick a new date.", "k": "when fast schedule week 4 8 12 dates calendar"}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Why we fast", "u": "fast-days.html#why-fast", "b": "Let the Field Rest  Rest for your gut A lighter day gives digestion a break, so your body can turn toward cleanup and repair. Supports your Reset Fasting builds on the habits and supplements you've already started. Fasting, made doable Portioned food means you're not just drinking water all day. Spaced out on purpose One day every 4 weeks, so your body adapts gradually.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Is fasting right for you?", "u": "fast-days.html#check-first", "b": "Safety First  Most patients do great. Tell us before your first fast if you: Are pregnant, trying to conceive, or breastfeeding Have diabetes or take blood sugar medication Take blood pressure medication Are underweight Have a history of disordered eating Have kidney or liver disease, or a heart condition Have a nut or soy allergy (check your kit's label) Are sick, or just started a new medication We may adjust your plan, give you personal instructions, or skip fasting for you. That's okay. Your Reset still works.", "k": "who should not fast pregnant diabetes safe contraindications"}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "The day before", "u": "fast-days.html#day-before", "b": "Prep  Eat a balanced dinner. Protein, vegetables and healthy fat. No heavy, greasy or late meal. No alcohol. Hydrate. Your usual glasses of water, plus one. Set out your kit so tomorrow is easy. Plan a calm day. Skip big events, hard workouts and long drives if you can.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Fast day rules", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-day-rules", "b": "The Day Of  Eat & Drink Only what's in your box No extra snacks or meals. Water, herbal tea and lemon water with a pinch of sea salt any time. Sip all day. 1 to 2 cups of black coffee or plain tea are fine. No milk, cream or sugar. Add an extra glass of water for each. Move Gently Walk and stretch Walking and stretching are perfect. Skip intense workouts, hot yoga and sauna today. Expect Some hunger is normal Some hunger, low energy or a mild headache is normal. It passes. Feeling a little tired or cold is common. Feeling unwell is not. Medications & supplements Keep taking Your prescription m", "k": "coffee allowed drink eat exercise rules"}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Medications & supplements", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-day-meds", "b": "Keep taking Your prescription medications, unless your provider told you otherwise. Pause for the day All your supplements. Restart the next morning with breakfast. Talk to us first If you take diabetes or blood pressure medication, you'll get personal instructions before your first fast.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Most fast-day headaches are thirst", "u": "fast-days.html#hydration-fast", "b": "Hydration Is Key  Start your morning with lemon water with sea salt: 8 to 12 oz water, juice of half a lemon, a pinch of sea salt. Sip, don't chug. A glass every hour or two. Aim for at least 8 glasses total. Herbal tea and lemon water count. Another lemon water with sea salt in the afternoon if you feel tired or get a headache. You're hydrated when your urine is pale yellow. Tips that make it easier Stay busy. A normal workday often goes faster than a free day. Warm drinks help. Herbal tea takes the edge off hunger. Get outside. A slow walk in fresh air resets your mood. Go to bed early. Slee", "k": "headache dizzy water fast"}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Tips that make it easier", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-tips", "b": "Stay busy. A normal workday often goes faster than a free day. Warm drinks help. Herbal tea takes the edge off hunger. Get outside. A slow walk in fresh air resets your mood. Go to bed early. Sleep is the easiest fasting hour. One day, then you're done.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "The day after", "u": "fast-days.html#day-after", "b": "Ease Back In  Break your fast gently. A light breakfast: eggs and vegetables, soup, or fruit with yogurt. Skip a big, heavy or sugary meal. Restart your supplements with breakfast. Note how you feel in Heads Up . A fast day can show a small weight drop. Most of it is water and returns. Fast day checklist Balanced dinner and no alcohol the night before Kit set out and meal plan read Water bottle filled Lemon water with sea salt first thing Prescription meds taken as usual Supplements paused for today Workout swapped for a walk Light breakfast planned for tomorrow", "k": "break fast breakfast after"}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Fast day checklist", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-checklist", "b": "Balanced dinner and no alcohol the night before Kit set out and meal plan read Water bottle filled Lemon water with sea salt first thing Prescription meds taken as usual Supplements paused for today Workout swapped for a walk Light breakfast planned for tomorrow", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Fast day questions", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq", "b": "Common Questions  Can I have coffee? Yes. 1 to 2 cups of black coffee or plain tea. No milk, cream or sugar. Add an extra glass of water for each cup. Do I have to eat the foods in order? Follow the order printed on your box as best you can. Spreading the food through the day keeps your energy steadier. I'm really hungry. Can I eat something else? Try warm herbal tea and lemon water with sea salt first. Hunger comes in waves and passes. If you feel dizzy, shaky or unwell, stop and eat. Your safety comes first. Can I work on a fast day? Yes. A normal workday often makes the day go faster. Avoid", "k": "fasting questions faq"}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Can I have coffee?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-coffee", "b": "Yes. 1 to 2 cups of black coffee or plain tea. No milk, cream or sugar. Add an extra glass of water for each cup.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Do I have to eat the foods in order?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-order", "b": "Follow the order printed on your box as best you can. Spreading the food through the day keeps your energy steadier.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "I'm really hungry. Can I eat something else?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-extra", "b": "Try warm herbal tea and lemon water with sea salt first. Hunger comes in waves and passes. If you feel dizzy, shaky or unwell, stop and eat. Your safety comes first.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Can I work on a fast day?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-work", "b": "Yes. A normal workday often makes the day go faster. Avoid long drives, big events and hard workouts if you can.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Can I fast on my period?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-period", "b": "Many women do fine. If your period makes you very tired or crampy, message us and we can move your fast a few days.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Do I take my medications and supplements?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-meds", "b": "Keep taking prescriptions unless we told you otherwise. Pause all your supplements and restart with breakfast the next morning.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "Why did the scale drop?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-weight", "b": "A fast day can show a small drop. Most of it is water and returns in a day or two. The real changes show up in your labs, your energy and how you feel.", "k": ""}, {"p": "ProLon Fast Guide", "t": "I broke my fast early. Did I ruin it?", "u": "fast-days.html#fast-faq-missed", "b": "No. You still gave your gut a rest. Note how you felt in Heads Up and tell us at your next check-in. We'll plan for an easier next one.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Blood draw guide", "u": "testing.html#blood-draw", "b": "Functional Labs  Your results are only as good as your prep. A few small steps help us read your labs clearly and build the right plan for you. 7 days Biotin & collagen hold Stop them a week before your draw. 7–10 AM Best time to draw Morning is best for hormones like testosterone and cortisol. Can't? Just note the time. Fasting Helpful, not required Unless your order says \"fasting required.\" If you ate, write down what and when. Supplement hold guide When What Why Stop 7 days before Biotin (B7), hair/skin/nail blends, collagen, creatine Biotin skews thyroid and hormone results. Creatine raise", "k": "labs blood work fasting prep bunny baseline"}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Supplement hold guide", "u": "testing.html#supplement-hold", "b": "When What Why Stop 7 days before Biotin (B7), hair/skin/nail blends, collagen, creatine Biotin skews thyroid and hormone results. Creatine raises creatinine, a kidney marker. Stop 24 hours before Iron supplements A recent dose can inflate your iron panel Hold the morning of All other non-essential supplements Bring them and take them right after your draw Keep taking Your prescription medications Unless your provider tells you otherwise (see special situations) 24 to 48 hours before Skip intense workouts. A walk is perfect. No alcohol for at least 24 hours. Hydrate well the day before. Morning", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "24 to 48 hours before", "u": "testing.html#before-draw", "b": "Skip intense workouts. A walk is perfect. No alcohol for at least 24 hours. Hydrate well the day before. Morning of, 1 to 2 glasses is plenty. Feeling sick or feverish? Reschedule.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Fasting draw?", "u": "testing.html#fasting-draw", "b": "Stop eating 8 to 12 hours before. Water only, plenty of it. Save coffee for after. Bring a snack for right after your draw. Couldn't fast? That's okay. Write down what you ate and when, and share it with us.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Special situations", "u": "testing.html#special-situations", "b": "Hormone creams or patches Apply estradiol and testosterone creams 4 to 6 hours before your draw, same timing every time. Have blood drawn from the arm you did not apply cream to. Patches: apply as you normally would. Oral progesterone Take your usual bedtime dose the night before. Thyroid medication Take your usual dose about 4 hours before your draw, if possible. Changed your dose? Wait 6 weeks before rechecking. Birth control pill Estrogen, progesterone and SHBG look different on the pill. That's expected. We read them in that context. GLP-1 / tirzepatide No need to skip your injection. If f", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Hormone creams or patches", "u": "testing.html#draw-hormone-cream", "b": "Apply estradiol and testosterone creams 4 to 6 hours before your draw, same timing every time. Have blood drawn from the arm you did not apply cream to. Patches: apply as you normally would.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Oral progesterone", "u": "testing.html#draw-progesterone", "b": "Take your usual bedtime dose the night before.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Thyroid medication", "u": "testing.html#draw-thyroid", "b": "Take your usual dose about 4 hours before your draw, if possible. Changed your dose? Wait 6 weeks before rechecking.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Birth control pill", "u": "testing.html#draw-birth-control", "b": "Estrogen, progesterone and SHBG look different on the pill. That's expected. We read them in that context.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "GLP-1 / tirzepatide", "u": "testing.html#draw-glp1", "b": "No need to skip your injection. If fasting, eat soon after your draw.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Men: PSA prep", "u": "testing.html#draw-psa", "b": "For 48 hours before, avoid ejaculation or sexual activity, cycling or spin, motorcycle or horseback riding, and heavy lifting. Tell us if you take finasteride or dutasteride, or had a recent prostate exam or procedure.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "What to bring", "u": "testing.html#what-to-bring", "b": "Photo ID and your lab order A current list of meds, supplements and herbs Your cycle day, if you menstruate (Day 1 = first day of your period) Draws are in-clinic at Lip Bunny Beauty, or at a remote Access location (additional draw fee).", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Morning-of checklist", "u": "testing.html#morning-checklist", "b": "Biotin, collagen & creatine stopped 7 days ago Iron held for 24 hours Other supplements packed for after Fasted, or noted what I ate and when 1 to 2 glasses of water this morning No alcohol or hard workout in 24 to 48 hrs Thyroid med ~4 hrs before (if applicable) Hormone cream 4 to 6 hrs before (if applicable) Photo ID in hand", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "After your draw", "u": "testing.html#after-draw", "b": "1 Draw day Book your results review before you leave. 2 We review Every marker, against standard and functional ranges. 3 Up to 10 business days Some results take time. We review carefully once everything is back. 4 Your review We walk through results and your plan together. Good to know One flagged number is not a diagnosis. We read the full pattern. Questions about your draw? Contact us, not the lab. We manage your order, results and next steps.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Gut health test", "u": "testing.html#gut-test", "b": "At-Home Kit · Tiny Health  A tiny swab with big insights. It maps the bacteria living in your gut: how well you digest, absorb and defend against inflammation. No spoons, no mess, about 5 minutes. Before you collect Antibiotics: wait 4 to 6 weeks after your last dose. Probiotics: pause probiotic supplements for 3 to 5 days. Food: eat like you normally do. We want a true picture. Prescriptions: keep taking them. How to collect Activate your kit first, using the QR code inside. When asked, choose your Lip Bunny provider. Wash your hands. After a bowel movement, wipe as usual with toilet paper. T", "k": "tiny health stool swab microbiome gut kit"}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Before you collect", "u": "testing.html#gut-before", "b": "Antibiotics: wait 4 to 6 weeks after your last dose. Probiotics: pause probiotic supplements for 3 to 5 days. Food: eat like you normally do. We want a true picture. Prescriptions: keep taking them.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "How to collect", "u": "testing.html#gut-collect", "b": "Activate your kit first, using the QR code inside. When asked, choose your Lip Bunny provider. Wash your hands. After a bowel movement, wipe as usual with toilet paper. Twist open the tube and remove the swab. Don't touch the tip. Swab the stool on the tissue until you see a small smudge on the tip. A tiny bit is plenty. Return the swab to its tube and close it tightly. Seal the tube in the specimen bag. Place it in the prepaid mailer and drop it in any USPS mailbox, the same or next day.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Vaginal health test", "u": "testing.html#vaginal-test", "b": "At-Home Kit · Tiny Health  Gentle, private and done in about 2 minutes. It maps the bacteria that protect your comfort, intimacy, fertility and hormone health. Before you collect 48 hours before: no sex and no lubricants. No douching, washes, or vaginal creams or suppositories. Timing: not during your period. Wait until bleeding stops. Medications: recent antibiotics or antifungals? Message us first. Keep taking prescriptions. Symptoms? Unusual discharge, odor, itching or pelvic pain? Call us first. You may need a visit. How to collect Activate your kit first. Choose your Lip Bunny provider. W", "k": "vaginal microbiome swab tiny health"}, {"p": "Testing & Labs", "t": "Saliva cortisol test", "u": "testing.html#cortisol-test", "b": "At-Home Kit · Access Labs  Cortisol should rise in the morning to wake you up and fall at night so you can sleep. Four saliva samples in one normal day show us your personal rhythm. 1 Morning Within 30 minutes of waking, before breakfast, coffee or brushing. 2 Noon Around 11 AM to 1 PM, before lunch. 3 Evening Around 4 to 6 PM, before dinner. 4 Night Around 10 PM to midnight, right before bed. Write the exact time on each tube. Kit times differ? Follow the kit. The day before No alcohol for 24 hours Skip licorice root and adaptogens (ashwagandha, rhodiola, holy basil) for 48 hours Skip hydroco", "k": "saliva cortisol stress adrenal access labs"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Your weekly GLP-1 injection", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#glp1-injection", "b": "Weight Loss · Metabolic Health  A once-weekly shot just under the skin. We'll walk you through your first one in the office. Use this page as your refresher at home. vial orange-cap syringe swabs sharps You'll need: your vial, an orange-cap insulin syringe, alcohol swabs and a sharps container. belly 2\" from navel thigh front/outer Pick your spot. Rotate every week. Avoid bruised, scarred or tattooed skin. 90° pinch · straight in · slow push Pinch a soft fold of skin and go straight in, at 90 degrees. Step 1 Draw up your dose Wash your hands. Wipe the vial stopper with alcohol. Let it dry. Pul", "k": "tirzepatide glp-1 shot injection weekly how to syringe vial"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Draw up your dose", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#draw-up", "b": "Step 1  Wash your hands. Wipe the vial stopper with alcohol. Let it dry. Pull air into the syringe equal to your dose. Push the air into the vial. Keep the needle in. Flip the vial upside down. Draw a little past your dose. Tap out any bubbles and push back to your exact dose in units , as written on your label.", "k": "draw up dose units air vial bubbles"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Give your injection", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#give-injection", "b": "Step 2  Wipe your spot with alcohol. Let it dry fully. Wet alcohol stings. Pinch a soft fold of skin. Insert the needle straight in, at 90 degrees. Let go of the pinch. Push the plunger slowly. Pull the needle out and press the swab gently. Don't rub. Drop the syringe straight into your sharps container.", "k": "give injection inject steps"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Storage & travel", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#storage", "b": "Keep it in the fridge. Never freeze it. Write the date on the vial the first time you use it. Discard 28 days later, even if some is left. Traveling? It can be out of the fridge up to 4 days. Keep it cool and out of the sun. Cloudy, has particles, or arrived warm? Don't use it. Call us.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Missed a dose?", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#missed-dose", "b": "Next dose more than 4 days away? Take it as soon as you remember. Next dose within 4 days? Skip it and stay on your normal day. Never double up. Missed 2+ weeks? Message us before restarting.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Needle disposal", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#sharps", "b": "In Massachusetts, needles can't go in the trash. Choose one: Order a sharps container from a pharmacy or online. Bring them to your next visit in a sharps container or a sealed heavy plastic bottle (like a detergent bottle). We'll dispose of them. Drop them at a local collection site.", "k": "needle disposal sharps container trash"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Side effects", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#glp-side-effects", "b": "Nausea Take a ginger supplement or sip ginger tea. Smaller meals, eaten slowly. Stop before you feel full. Skip greasy foods. Constipation Magnesium glycinate in the evening with plenty of fluids, as directed. Eat 2 prunes or dates daily. Keep up your fiber and water. Digestion Better Bitters spray 10 minutes before meals. Good to know Small redness or a bump where you injected is common and fades in a day or two. On birth control pills? We recommend adding a second form of birth control, like condoms. Pregnant or planning to be? Stop and tell us right away. GLP-1s haven't been studied in preg", "k": "nausea constipation side effects glp-1 digestion"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Hormone therapy", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#hormones", "b": "Bioidentical · Women  How to use your hormones, what to expect, and how we keep you safe. Your plan may use one, two or all three. Cream · Patch · Vaginal Estrogen Hot flashes and night sweats Vaginal and urinary comfort Bone, mood and skin support Capsule at bedtime Progesterone Balances estrogen Protects the uterine lining Deeper, calmer sleep Cream Testosterone Libido and desire Energy and motivation Mental clarity and strength Applying your creams Where: inner thigh, inner arm or abdomen. Rotate spots every day. Clean, dry skin. Let it dry before dressing. Wash your hands right after apply", "k": "hrt bioidentical estrogen estradiol progesterone testosterone cream menopause"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Applying your creams", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#applying-creams", "b": "Where: inner thigh, inner arm or abdomen. Rotate spots every day. Clean, dry skin. Let it dry before dressing. Wash your hands right after applying. Protect others from transfer Keep the area covered with clothing. Apply at least 8 hours before intimacy, or after. Keep children and pets away from treated skin.", "k": "apply cream where transfer"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Vaginal estrogen", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#vaginal-estrogen", "b": "Works best applied after intimacy, so it doesn't transfer to your partner.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Testosterone: vulvar option", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#testosterone-vulvar", "b": "If your provider recommends it, it can be applied to the clitoris and labia in the morning or after intimacy. Start 2 days a week here and use your usual spots on other days. Watch for clitoral enlargement. If it happens, stop vulvar use and call us.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Taking progesterone", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#progesterone", "b": "At bedtime. It can make you sleepy. With a little healthy fat, like a spoonful of almond butter, for better absorption. No period for 3+ months? Take it every night. Still having periods? Cycle it, as shown, unless told otherwise. Peanut allergy? Tell us. Some capsules contain peanut oil. Who needs progesterone? Uterus + estrogen: required, to protect your lining Partial hysterectomy (cervix kept): required Mirena IUD in place: oral progesterone not required Full hysterectomy: not required, but highly recommended Day 1 first day of bleeding Day 15 start nightly Day 29 stop Cycling schedule. A ", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "What to expect", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#hrt-expect", "b": "Wk 1–2 Your body is adjusting. Changes may be subtle. Wk 3–4 Early improvements in sleep, energy or mood. Wk 6–8 Fewer hot flashes, better libido, clearer thinking. ~3 mo Your plan is fine-tuned based on how you feel and your labs. Your follow-up plan 4 to 6 weeks after starting or any dose change: labs and a check-in Once stable: labs at least every 6 months Every year: your full initial panel Hormone labs don't require fasting. See blood draw timing for creams . Staying safe Pelvic ultrasound every 5 years is recommended to check your uterine lining. Keep up with mammograms and routine scree", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Your follow-up plan", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#hrt-follow-up", "b": "4 to 6 weeks after starting or any dose change: labs and a check-in Once stable: labs at least every 6 months Every year: your full initial panel Hormone labs don't require fasting. See blood draw timing for creams .", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Staying safe", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#hrt-safety", "b": "Pelvic ultrasound every 5 years is recommended to check your uterine lining. Keep up with mammograms and routine screenings. Missed a dose? Skip it. Never double up. Never change your dose without talking to us. Testosterone and pregnancy: pregnant, might be, or trying to conceive? Stop testosterone and call us. Not for use while breastfeeding.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "GHK-Cu: the copper peptide", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#ghk-cu", "b": "Skin · Hair · Longevity  GHK-Cu is a naturally occurring peptide that binds to copper. It may help support the body's natural repair environment and the proteins involved in firmness, texture and follicle health. Shipped cold Compounded and delivered to your door. Keep refrigerated Temperature-sensitive. Consistency matters more than amount. 8–12 weeks Typical time to see results. Skin · Topical serum How to use Apply after cleansing, to dry skin. Wait about 10 minutes before moisturizer. Rotate every other day with other actives (like retinol). Use mineral sunscreen daily. Stop if it burns or", "k": "copper peptide skin hair serum scalp"}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "How to use", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#ghk-skin", "b": "Skin · Topical serum  Apply after cleansing, to dry skin. Wait about 10 minutes before moisturizer. Rotate every other day with other actives (like retinol). Use mineral sunscreen daily. Stop if it burns or stings for long in the sun.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "How to use", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#ghk-hair", "b": "Hair · Scalp solution  Apply to a clean, dry scalp once daily. No rinsing needed. Part hair in sections for even coverage. Avoid heat styling right after applying. Store refrigerated.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "t": "Injectables & IV drips", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html#iv-injectables", "b": "Also at Lip Bunny  B12/MIC, glutathione and NAD+ injections, plus IV drips, are available in the clinic. Ask at your next visit whether one fits your plan.", "k": "b12 nad glutathione iv drip injection"}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Get set up in Heads Up", "u": "tracker.html#get-started", "b": "Step One  Heads Up is your tracker for the whole program. Your care team sees what you log, so we can adjust your plan between visits. Watch for your invite. We send it by email when you join. Check your spam folder if you don't see it. Download the Heads Up Health app. Search \"Heads Up Health\" in your phone's app store, then sign in with the email from your invite. Connect your devices if you have them, like a scale, watch or sleep tracker. This is optional. Log your first entry before your results review. Can't find your invite? Contact the office and we'll resend it.", "k": "heads up health app download invite login account tracker"}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "What to log", "u": "tracker.html#what-to-log", "b": "Keep It Simple  A few minutes a day is plenty. Done is better than perfect. Every day Any symptoms, and your habits: water, movement, sunlight and supplements. You can also track your weight here if you like. Once a week Rate your energy, sleep, digestion, mood and bloating. Pick the same day each week so the trend is easy to read. Gut and pH Bowel movements per day (goal: at least 1). Morning pH if you are checking it. Fast days Log how you felt during and after each ProLon fast. See the ProLon Fast Guide . Wins and questions Note wins, food reactions and questions for your next visit. We rev", "k": "log weight symptoms energy sleep digestion mood bloating bowel movements ph habits"}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Every day", "u": "tracker.html#log-daily", "b": "Any symptoms, and your habits: water, movement, sunlight and supplements. You can also track your weight here if you like.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Once a week", "u": "tracker.html#log-weekly", "b": "Rate your energy, sleep, digestion, mood and bloating. Pick the same day each week so the trend is easy to read.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Gut and pH", "u": "tracker.html#log-gut", "b": "Bowel movements per day (goal: at least 1). Morning pH if you are checking it.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Fast days", "u": "tracker.html#log-fast", "b": "Log how you felt during and after each ProLon fast. See the ProLon Fast Guide .", "k": ""}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Wins and questions", "u": "tracker.html#log-notes", "b": "Note wins, food reactions and questions for your next visit. We review them with you.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Lab trends", "u": "tracker.html#log-labs", "b": "When your labs are added, you can see your progress over time, from first labs to recheck.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Track in Heads Up", "t": "Tips for logging", "u": "tracker.html#tips", "b": "Make It Stick  Set a daily reminder on your phone, like right after your morning mineral water. Missed a day? Just pick up again. No need to catch up. Before each visit, open Heads Up and look at your week. Bring your questions. Heads Up is not for emergencies We don't watch it around the clock. No bowel movement for 2+ days, or reactions more than mild? Reach out . In an emergency, call 911.", "k": "reminder habit consistency"}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "About the program", "u": "faq.html#faq-program", "b": "The Program  Why start with a Reset instead of medication? Medication works best on a balanced foundation. The Reset shifts your baseline first. Some patients find they need less medication, or none at all. Others start GLP-1 or hormones with fewer side effects. Is my program 8 or 16 weeks? Every program runs 16 weeks with a full recheck at the end. Your Tiny Health gut test score decides how long your intensive Reset phase lasts: 8 weeks if your score is over 80, the full 16 weeks if it's under 80. The price is the same either way, because we don't believe in charging you more for needing mor", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Why start with a Reset instead of medication?", "u": "faq.html#why-not-medication-first", "b": "Medication works best on a balanced foundation. The Reset shifts your baseline first. Some patients find they need less medication, or none at all. Others start GLP-1 or hormones with fewer side effects.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Is my program 8 or 16 weeks?", "u": "faq.html#how-long", "b": "Every program runs 16 weeks with a full recheck at the end. Your Tiny Health gut test score decides how long your intensive Reset phase lasts: 8 weeks if your score is over 80, the full 16 weeks if it's under 80. The price is the same either way, because we don't believe in charging you more for needing more time.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Why test the gut?", "u": "faq.html#why-gut-test", "b": "Research continues to link gut health to hormones, inflammation, mood and metabolism. Testing at the start and the end shows how your gut responded to the program.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Can I start with hormones or GLP-1?", "u": "faq.html#start-hrt-glp", "b": "Every journey starts with the Reset. If hormones or lean body mass are part of your goals, we look at whether you're ready around week 8, based on your labs and symptoms. Hormone therapy is offered to women only.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Are visits in person or virtual?", "u": "faq.html#in-person", "b": "Program visits and blood draws are in person at Lip Bunny Beauty in Fall River, MA. Some follow-up visits can be virtual.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Is the program open to men?", "u": "faq.html#men", "b": "Yes. The Reset, Hoptimization, GLP-1, testing, injectables and IV therapy are all available to men. Bioidentical hormone therapy is offered for women only.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "How do I pay?", "u": "faq.html#payment", "b": "A $200 deposit holds your spot and goes toward your program. The balance is due to start. Financing is available through Cherry and CareCredit. Our front desk can walk you through it.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "What's included?", "u": "faq.html#whats-included", "b": "Your Bunny Baseline blood work at the start and graduation, Tiny Health gut tests, your customized supplement plan, ProLon fast kits, your visits and check-ins, a Styku body scan, the Heads Up app, and SweatEnergy. Add-on protocols, if recommended, are priced separately.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Living the Reset", "u": "faq.html#faq-daily", "b": "Day to Day  I feel worse, not better. Is that normal? In the first few days of a new step, mild tiredness, fogginess, a mild headache or digestion changes can be normal. Hydrate, make sure you're having daily bowel movements, and rest. Reach out if it's more than mild or lasts more than a few days. See quick help . I slipped up. Did I ruin it? No. Missing a day doesn't undo anything. Just restart the next meal or the next morning. Consistency over weeks is what counts, not perfection over days. Can I still drink coffee? Yes, in moderation. Have your lemon water with sea salt first, and add an ", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "I feel worse, not better. Is that normal?", "u": "faq.html#feel-worse", "b": "In the first few days of a new step, mild tiredness, fogginess, a mild headache or digestion changes can be normal. Hydrate, make sure you're having daily bowel movements, and rest. Reach out if it's more than mild or lasts more than a few days. See quick help .", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "I slipped up. Did I ruin it?", "u": "faq.html#slip-up", "b": "No. Missing a day doesn't undo anything. Just restart the next meal or the next morning. Consistency over weeks is what counts, not perfection over days.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Can I still drink coffee?", "u": "faq.html#coffee", "b": "Yes, in moderation. Have your lemon water with sea salt first, and add an extra glass of water for each cup. Keep it black or with a clean milk. On fast days, 1 to 2 cups of black coffee or plain tea are fine.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Can I drink alcohol?", "u": "faq.html#alcohol", "b": "We recommend taking a break, or at least moderating it. Alcohol adds to the load your liver is working to clear. No alcohol the day before a fast day or a blood draw.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "How do I eat out?", "u": "faq.html#eating-out", "b": "Pick a protein and vegetables, ask for olive oil and lemon instead of creamy dressings, skip the fried sides, and use your bitters before a heavy meal. Then enjoy it. It's 80%, not 100%.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Should I exercise?", "u": "faq.html#exercise", "b": "Yes. Daily walking first, then strength work. Use your included SweatEnergy subscription for workouts. Skip hard workouts on fast days and during a rough patch. Sweat 2 to 4 times a week if you tolerate it, and rehydrate with electrolytes.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Will the program affect my cycle?", "u": "faq.html#period", "b": "Changes in stress, food, sleep and weight can shift your cycle a little. Note it in Heads Up and tell us at your next visit. Tell us right away if you might be pregnant.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Supplements & meds", "u": "faq.html#faq-meds", "b": "Supplements & Medications  Do I stop my prescriptions? No. Never stop a prescription without talking to us or the prescriber first. Keep fiber and binders at least 2 hours away from your medications. When do my supplements start? After your results review (program week 1). Before then, focus on your first habits: hydration, electrolytes and sleep. What if I get pregnant during the program? Stop your supplements and any GLP-1 or testosterone, and call us right away. Some herbs and medications aren't safe in pregnancy. We'll adjust your plan. I have surgery or a dental procedure coming up. Tell ", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Do I stop my prescriptions?", "u": "faq.html#faq-prescriptions", "b": "No. Never stop a prescription without talking to us or the prescriber first. Keep fiber and binders at least 2 hours away from your medications.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "When do my supplements start?", "u": "faq.html#faq-when-supplements", "b": "After your results review (program week 1). Before then, focus on your first habits: hydration, electrolytes and sleep.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "What if I get pregnant during the program?", "u": "faq.html#faq-pregnant", "b": "Stop your supplements and any GLP-1 or testosterone, and call us right away. Some herbs and medications aren't safe in pregnancy. We'll adjust your plan.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "I have surgery or a dental procedure coming up.", "u": "faq.html#faq-surgery", "b": "Tell us as soon as it's scheduled. Some supplements need to be paused 1 to 2 weeks before a procedure.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "My doctor started a new medication.", "u": "faq.html#faq-new-med", "b": "Message us with the name and dose. We'll check it against your supplements and your plan.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "Scheduling & results", "u": "faq.html#faq-office", "b": "The Office  When will I get my results? Blood work can take up to 10 business days to come back, and we take time to review every marker. Gut tests take about 4 weeks. We'll go through everything with you at your results review. How do I reschedule? Call us at (508) 388-2200 or message us in the Symplast for Patients app. Our front desk books your next step before you leave every visit. How do I message my provider? Use the Symplast for Patients app (free on iPhone and Android). It's where your lab review, messages and appointments live. For anything urgent, call. For emergencies, call 911. My", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "When will I get my results?", "u": "faq.html#faq-results", "b": "Blood work can take up to 10 business days to come back, and we take time to review every marker. Gut tests take about 4 weeks. We'll go through everything with you at your results review.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "How do I reschedule?", "u": "faq.html#faq-reschedule", "b": "Call us at (508) 388-2200 or message us in the Symplast for Patients app. Our front desk books your next step before you leave every visit.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "How do I message my provider?", "u": "faq.html#faq-message", "b": "Use the Symplast for Patients app (free on iPhone and Android). It's where your lab review, messages and appointments live. For anything urgent, call. For emergencies, call 911.", "k": ""}, {"p": "FAQ", "t": "My question isn't here.", "u": "faq.html#faq-not-answered", "b": "Try the search at the top of any page, or contact us . We'd always rather hear from you.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Contact Us", "t": "Symplast for Patients", "u": "contact.html#message-provider", "b": "Message your provider  Your lab review, results, messages and appointments in one place. Free on iPhone and Android. Search \"Symplast for Patients\" in your app store.", "k": ""}, {"p": "Contact Us", "t": "Lip Bunny Beauty", "u": "contact.html#visit", "b": "Visit us  484 Highland Ave, Fall River, MA Please arrive 15 minutes early to your first visit. Get directions", "k": ""}, {"p": "Contact Us", "t": "Who to contact for what", "u": "contact.html#who-to-contact", "b": "The Right Door  I need to… Best way Book, move or cancel a visit Call the office Ask about payment or financing Call the office Ask a question about my plan, supplements or symptoms Message your provider in the Symplast app See my lab review or results Symplast for Patients app Report a reaction that's more than mild Call the office, then message with details Reorder supplements after my program Call the office to pick up at Lip Bunny, or order on Fullscript Learn about the program or tell a friend The Wellness Hunny website Something feels like an emergency Call 911 or go to the nearest ER", "k": ""}, {"p": "Contact Us", "t": "Start your journey", "u": "contact.html#new-patients", "b": "Not a Patient Yet?  Learn about the program, pricing and testing on our main website. Visit The Wellness Hunny →", "k": ""}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Start Here", "u": "start-here.html", "b": "The why behind everything you'll do. Read this first, then come back whenever you need a reminder.", "k": "Start Here"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Your Program", "u": "your-program.html", "b": "What happens, when it happens, and what your job is at each step.", "k": "Your Program"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Daily Habits", "u": "daily-habits.html", "b": "One habit at a time, in order. This is the real protocol.", "k": "Daily Habits"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Food & Recipes", "u": "food.html", "b": "What to lean into, what to take a break from, and easy meals for real life.", "k": "Food"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Natural Remedies", "u": "remedies.html", "b": "Baths, teas, herbs, binders and simple swaps that support your body between visits.", "k": "Natural Remedies"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Supplements", "u": "supplements.html", "b": "What each one does, when to take it, and the rules that keep you safe.", "k": "Supplements"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "ProLon Fast Guide", "u": "fast-days.html", "b": "Everything you need for an easy fast day: the day before, the day of, and the day after.", "k": "Fast Days"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Testing & Labs", "u": "testing.html", "b": "How to prepare for your blood draw and how to collect your at-home kits.", "k": "Testing"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Lip Bunny Rx Patient Guides", "u": "lip-bunny-rx.html", "b": "How-to guides for patients on GLP-1 injections, bioidentical hormones, and GHK-Cu. Always follow the dose on your label.", "k": "Lip Bunny Rx"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Track in Heads Up", "u": "tracker.html", "b": "Heads Up is where you track your symptoms and habits, and your weight if you like. Your care team sees it and uses it at every visit.", "k": "Heads Up"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "FAQ", "u": "faq.html", "b": "Quick answers to what patients ask us most.", "k": "FAQ"}, {"p": "Page", "t": "Contact Us", "u": "contact.html", "b": "Questions, scheduling, or something doesn't feel right? Reach out. We'd always rather hear from you.", "k": "Contact"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Bunny Overnight Chia", "u": "food.html#r-overnight-chia", "b": "Ingredients: 3 tbsp chia seeds, 3/4 cup milk of choice (almond, coconut or oat), A handful of frozen raspberries, 1 tbsp dark chocolate chips, 1 tbsp pumpkin seeds, 1 spoonful almond butter", "k": "recipe Breakfast"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Chia Pudding with Fruit", "u": "food.html#r-chia-pudding", "b": "Ingredients: 3 tbsp chia seeds, 3/4 cup almond or coconut milk, 1/2 tsp vanilla, Pinch of cinnamon, 1/2 cup berries or diced mango, Optional: 1 tsp raw honey", "k": "recipe Breakfast"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Veggie Scramble", "u": "food.html#r-veggie-scramble", "b": "Ingredients: 2 to 3 pasture-raised eggs, 1 large handful spinach, 1/4 onion or 2 green onions, chopped, Optional: peppers, mushrooms or tomatoes, 1 tsp olive oil or butter, 1/2 avocado, sliced, Sea salt, pepper, fresh herbs", "k": "recipe Breakfast"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Eggs, Greens & Sweet Potato Hash", "u": "food.html#r-eggs-greens-hash", "b": "Ingredients: 1 medium sweet potato, small cubes, 1/2 onion, diced, 2 big handfuls kale or spinach, 4 eggs, 1 tbsp olive oil, Sea salt, pepper, paprika, Optional: 1/2 avocado", "k": "recipe Breakfast"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Herb Veggie Omelet", "u": "food.html#r-veggie-omelet", "b": "Ingredients: 2 to 3 eggs, 1/4 cup chopped veggies (peppers, spinach, mushrooms, onion), 1 tbsp fresh herbs (parsley, basil, chives), 1 tsp olive oil or butter, Sea salt and pepper", "k": "recipe Breakfast"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Smoothie Bowl", "u": "food.html#r-smoothie-bowl", "b": "Ingredients: 1 cup frozen berries or mango, 1/2 frozen banana, 1/2 cup almond milk or coconut yogurt, Optional: 1 scoop protein powder or collagen, Toppings: 2 tbsp granola, 1 tbsp hemp or chia seeds, fresh fruit", "k": "recipe Breakfast"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Big Salad with Lemon-Olive Oil Dressing", "u": "food.html#r-big-salad", "b": "Ingredients: 2 big handfuls mixed greens, Cucumber, carrots, peppers, any raw veggies, 1/4 avocado, 1 tbsp seeds or nuts, Fresh parsley or basil, Protein: 4 to 5 oz grilled chicken, salmon or shrimp, Dressing: 2 tbsp olive oil, juice of 1/2 lemon, 1/2 tsp Dijon, pinch of sea salt", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Salmon Salad over Greens", "u": "food.html#r-salmon-salad", "b": "Ingredients: 1 can (5 to 6 oz) wild salmon, or leftover baked salmon, 2 tbsp plain Greek yogurt or avocado-oil mayo, 1 tsp Dijon, 1 celery stalk, diced, 1 tbsp chopped dill or parsley, Juice of 1/2 lemon, Mixed greens to serve", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Herb Chicken Salad", "u": "food.html#r-chicken-salad", "b": "Ingredients: 2 cups cooked chicken, chopped, 1 celery stalk, diced, 1/4 cup red grapes or apple, chopped, 2 tbsp olive oil, Juice of 1/2 lemon, 1 tbsp fresh parsley, Mixed greens or lettuce cups", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Turkey Lettuce Wraps", "u": "food.html#r-lettuce-wraps", "b": "Ingredients: 1/2 lb ground turkey, 1 tsp olive oil, 1 garlic clove, minced, 1 tsp grated ginger, 1 tbsp coconut aminos, 1 carrot and 1/2 cucumber, matchsticks, Butter or romaine lettuce leaves, Fresh cilantro", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Lentil Soup", "u": "food.html#r-lentil-soup", "b": "Ingredients: 1 tbsp olive oil, 1 onion, 2 carrots, 2 celery stalks, diced, 2 garlic cloves, 1 cup dry lentils, rinsed, 6 cups broth, 1 can diced tomatoes, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp thyme, 2 handfuls spinach, Juice of 1/2 lemon", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Veggie Soup", "u": "food.html#r-veggie-soup", "b": "Ingredients: 1 tbsp olive oil, 1 onion, 2 carrots, 2 celery stalks, diced, 3 garlic cloves, 2 cups chopped cabbage or kale, 1 zucchini, diced, 6 cups broth, 1 tsp turmeric, 1 tsp thyme, Fresh parsley and lemon", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Turkey & Veggie Soup", "u": "food.html#r-turkey-veggie-soup", "b": "Ingredients: 1 lb ground turkey, 1 tbsp olive oil, 1 onion, 2 carrots, 2 celery stalks, diced, 2 garlic cloves, 1 zucchini, diced, 1 can diced tomatoes, 6 cups broth, 1 tsp oregano, 1 tsp thyme, 2 handfuls spinach", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Quinoa Bowl with Roasted Veggies & Chickpeas", "u": "food.html#r-quinoa-bowl", "b": "Ingredients: 1/2 cup quinoa, 2 cups chopped veggies (sweet potato, broccoli, peppers, red onion), 1 can chickpeas, rinsed and dried, 2 tbsp olive oil, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp paprika, Handful of parsley, Lemon-tahini or lemon-olive oil dressing", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Lentil & Veggie Bowl", "u": "food.html#r-lentil-bowl", "b": "Ingredients: 1 cup cooked lentils (or 1 can, rinsed), 2 cups roasted or sautéed veggies, 2 handfuls greens, 1/4 avocado, Pumpkin seeds, Lemon-olive oil dressing, Fresh herbs", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Baked Salmon & Veggies", "u": "food.html#r-salmon-sheet-pan", "b": "Ingredients: 2 wild salmon fillets (5 to 6 oz each), 1 head broccoli in florets, or 1 bunch asparagus, 2 tbsp olive oil, 1 lemon, 2 garlic cloves, minced, Sea salt, pepper, dill, Side: quinoa or a baked sweet potato", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Baked Cod with Roasted Veggies", "u": "food.html#r-baked-cod", "b": "Ingredients: 2 cod fillets, 3 cups brussels sprouts (halved) or cabbage wedges, 2 tbsp olive oil, 1 lemon, 1 tsp paprika, 1 tsp garlic powder, Fresh parsley, Side: quinoa or wild rice", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Stir-Fry (Chicken, Tofu or Shrimp)", "u": "food.html#r-stir-fry", "b": "Ingredients: 10 oz chicken strips, firm tofu cubes, or shrimp, 4 cups mixed veggies (broccoli, peppers, snap peas, carrots), 1 tbsp avocado oil, 2 garlic cloves, 1 tsp ginger, Sauce: 3 tbsp coconut aminos, 1 tsp toasted sesame oil, 1 tsp rice vinegar, Cooked rice to serve, Green onion, sesame seeds", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Shrimp Tacos with Cilantro Slaw", "u": "food.html#r-shrimp-tacos", "b": "Ingredients: 1/2 lb shrimp, peeled, 1 tsp chili powder, 1/2 tsp cumin, garlic powder, 1 tbsp olive oil, 6 corn tortillas, Slaw: 2 cups shredded cabbage, handful cilantro, juice of 1 lime, 1 tbsp olive oil, pinch of salt, Avocado, lime wedges", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Herb-Roasted Chicken Thighs", "u": "food.html#r-herb-chicken", "b": "Ingredients: 6 bone-in or boneless chicken thighs, 2 tbsp olive oil, 1 tbsp fresh thyme, 1 tbsp fresh rosemary (or 1 tsp each dried), 3 garlic cloves, minced, 1 lemon, 1 bunch asparagus or 4 carrots, cut, Side: wild rice or quinoa", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Turkey Meatballs with Zucchini Noodles", "u": "food.html#r-turkey-meatballs", "b": "Ingredients: 1 lb ground turkey, 1 egg, 2 tbsp almond flour, 2 garlic cloves, minced, 1 tbsp each fresh basil and oregano (or 1 tsp dried), 1 jar clean marinara (no added sugar or seed oils), 3 to 4 zucchini, spiralized", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Burger in a Lettuce Wrap", "u": "food.html#r-turkey-burger", "b": "Ingredients: 1 lb grass-fed beef or ground turkey, 1 tsp garlic powder, 1 tsp onion powder, salt, pepper, Large lettuce leaves, Tomato, red onion, pickles, avocado, Side salad, Sauerkraut on the side", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Leftover Bowl", "u": "food.html#r-meatball-bowl", "b": "Ingredients: Leftover meatballs or burger patty, 1/2 cup rice or quinoa, 2 handfuls greens, Any raw or roasted veggies, Dressing or a spoon of marinara", "k": "recipe Lunch"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Chicken Fajita Bowl", "u": "food.html#r-fajita-bowl", "b": "Ingredients: 2 chicken breasts, sliced into strips, 2 bell peppers and 1 onion, sliced, 1 tbsp olive oil, 1 tsp chili powder, 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp paprika, 1 cup cooked rice, Avocado, salsa, fresh cilantro, lime", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Celebration Dinner", "u": "food.html#r-celebration-dinner", "b": "Ingredients: Anything you love, Good company, No guilt", "k": "recipe Dinner"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Bunny Green Smoothie", "u": "food.html#r-bunny-green", "b": "Ingredients: 1 big handful spinach, 1/2 cucumber, 1/2 green apple, Juice of 1/2 lemon, Small handful parsley, 1 cup filtered water, Ice", "k": "recipe Smoothie · Liver support"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Berry Antioxidant Smoothie", "u": "food.html#r-berry-antioxidant", "b": "Ingredients: 1 cup frozen mixed berries, 1/2 cup coconut yogurt, 1 tbsp chia seeds, 1 cup almond milk", "k": "recipe Smoothie · Antioxidants"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Tropical Gut Reset Smoothie", "u": "food.html#r-tropical-gut", "b": "Ingredients: 1/2 cup frozen pineapple, 1/2 cup frozen mango, 1 tsp fresh ginger, 1 cup coconut water, A few fresh mint leaves", "k": "recipe Smoothie · Digestion"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Creamy Cacao Smoothie", "u": "food.html#r-creamy-cacao", "b": "Ingredients: 1 frozen banana, 1 tbsp cacao powder, 1 tbsp almond butter, 1 cup almond milk, Pinch of cinnamon", "k": "recipe Smoothie · Energy"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Beet and Berry Smoothie", "u": "food.html#r-beet-berry", "b": "Ingredients: 1 small cooked beet, 1/2 cup blueberries, 1/2 frozen banana, 1 cup almond milk, 1 tsp fresh ginger", "k": "recipe Smoothie · Circulation"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Golden Turmeric Smoothie", "u": "food.html#r-golden-turmeric", "b": "Ingredients: 1 cup frozen mango, 1/2 tsp turmeric, Pinch of black pepper, 1 cup coconut milk, 1 tsp raw honey", "k": "recipe Smoothie · Inflammation"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Energy Bites", "u": "food.html#r-energy-bites", "b": "Ingredients: 1 cup pitted dates, 1/2 cup almond butter, 2 tbsp chia seeds, 1 tsp cinnamon, Optional: 2 tbsp dark chocolate chips or shredded coconut", "k": "recipe Sweet Treat"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Frozen Banana Bites", "u": "food.html#r-banana-bites", "b": "Ingredients: 2 bananas, sliced into rounds, 1/3 cup dark chocolate (70%+), Pinch of flaky sea salt", "k": "recipe Sweet Treat"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Baked Cinnamon Apples", "u": "food.html#r-cinnamon-apples", "b": "Ingredients: 2 apples, sliced, 1 tsp cinnamon, 1 tsp raw honey or maple syrup, 1 tsp butter or coconut oil, Optional: chopped walnuts", "k": "recipe Sweet Treat"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Chia Pudding Cups", "u": "food.html#r-chia-cups", "b": "Ingredients: 1/3 cup chia seeds, 1 1/2 cups almond milk, 1 tsp vanilla, 1 tsp maple syrup, Berries to top", "k": "recipe Sweet Treat"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Berries + Coconut Whip", "u": "food.html#r-berries-whip", "b": "Ingredients: 1 can full-fat coconut milk, chilled overnight, 1/2 tsp vanilla, 1 cup mixed berries", "k": "recipe Sweet Treat"}, {"p": "Recipe", "t": "Dark Chocolate + Sea Salt", "u": "food.html#r-dark-chocolate", "b": "Ingredients: 1 to 2 squares dark chocolate, 70%+ cacao, Pinch of flaky sea salt", "k": "recipe Sweet Treat"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Methyl Protect (XYMOGEN)", "u": "supplements.html#s-methyl-protect", "b": "Active B vitamins (folate, B12, B6, B2) plus TMG that support methylation, energy, mood and detox pathways. When: Morning, with breakfast. Start low. Your provider may increase it after 2 weeks. Morning is best. B vitamins can be energizing.", "k": "supplement Foundation"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Vitamin D3 5000 + K (Metagenics)", "u": "supplements.html#s-vitamin-d-5000", "b": "Vitamin D3 with vitamin K1 and K2 for immunity, mood, hormones and bones. K helps send calcium to your bones. When: Morning or midday, with a meal that has healthy fat. Take it with fat (eggs, avocado, olive oil, nuts) for best absorption. Morning is better than night. Vitamin D late in the day can affect sleep for some people. Your strength is matched to your vitamin D lab level. We recheck it.", "k": "supplement Foundation"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Vitamin D3 10,000 + K (Metagenics)", "u": "supplements.html#s-vitamin-d-10000", "b": "A higher-strength vitamin D3 with K1 and K2, used short term when labs show a bigger deficiency. When: Morning or midday, with a meal that has healthy fat. Take it with fat for best absorption. This is a short-term repletion strength. We recheck your level and step you down when it's back in range.", "k": "supplement Foundation"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Magnesium Glycinate 350 (Solaray)", "u": "supplements.html#s-magnesium-glycinate", "b": "A calming, gentle form of magnesium for sleep, stress, muscles and regular bowel movements. When: Evening or bedtime. Start with 1 capsule and build up. Loose stools mean drop back to the last dose that felt good. Take 4 hours apart from thyroid medication. Space 2 hours from certain antibiotics (tetracyclines, fluoroquinolones).", "k": "supplement Foundation"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "GLP-1 Daily Support Fiber (Vital Nutrients)", "u": "supplements.html#s-glp1-fiber", "b": "A gentle prebiotic fiber that feeds good gut bacteria, keeps you regular, steadies blood sugar and helps you feel full. When: With lunch, mixed in 8 to 10 oz of water. Week 1: half a scoop. Then a full scoop. Drink a full glass of water with it. Fiber needs water to work. Gas or bloating at first is common and usually settles in a week.", "k": "supplement Foundation"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Classic Better Bitters (Herb Pharm)", "u": "supplements.html#s-better-bitters", "b": "A bitter herbal spray that wakes up digestion: stomach acid, bile and enzymes. When: 10 to 15 minutes before heavier meals (meat, dairy, foods that bloat you). Hold it in your mouth briefly. Tasting the bitterness is how it works. Use 1 to 2 times a day, before your biggest meals.", "k": "supplement Foundation"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Liver-G.I. Detox (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-liver-gi-detox", "b": "Supports both phases of liver detox and gut cleansing with milk thistle, NAC, turmeric, artichoke, broccoli sprout and chlorella. When: Morning, with breakfast. Liver pathways run well in the morning. Pair it with breakfast.", "k": "supplement Detox & Liver"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "DIM Detox (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-dim-detox", "b": "Supports healthy estrogen metabolism and phase II liver detox with DIM, calcium-D-glucarate, broccoli sprout and milk thistle. When: With meals. Take with food to avoid an upset stomach.", "k": "supplement Detox & Liver"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "PectaClear Detox Formula (EcoNugenics)", "u": "supplements.html#s-pectaclear", "b": "A gentle binder of modified citrus pectin and kelp alginate that grabs toxins and heavy metals so they leave your body. When: On waking, on an empty stomach with water. Binders work best on an empty stomach. Keep it at least 2 hours away from food, medications and other supplements. Daily bowel movements are a must while taking a binder.", "k": "supplement Detox & Liver"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Liposomal Glutathione (Quicksilver Scientific)", "u": "supplements.html#s-liposomal-glutathione", "b": "Your body's master antioxidant in a liposomal liquid for better absorption. When: Empty stomach, at least 10 minutes before a meal. Hold it in your mouth for 30 seconds before swallowing. Refrigerate after opening. Use within 30 days.", "k": "supplement Detox & Liver"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "NAC + Glycine Powder (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-nac-glycine", "b": "The two building blocks your body uses to make glutathione, for antioxidant, immune and detox support. When: Daytime, mixed in 8 oz of water. Stir well. It has a slight sulfur taste from the NAC. Use within 120 days of opening.", "k": "supplement Detox & Liver"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Turmeric Supreme Joint (Gaia Herbs)", "u": "supplements.html#s-turmeric-supreme-joint", "b": "Turmeric with boswellia, devil's claw, ginger, quercetin and black pepper for joint comfort and a healthy inflammatory response. When: With meals. Food (especially fat) helps you absorb turmeric. Benefits build over a few weeks of steady use.", "k": "supplement Heart & Joints"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Arterosil HP (Calroy Health Sciences)", "u": "supplements.html#s-arterosil", "b": "Supports the inner lining of your blood vessels (the glycocalyx) with a green seaweed extract and fruit and vegetable polyphenols. When: Morning and evening, with meals. Split morning and evening for steady support.", "k": "supplement Heart & Joints"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "CoQ10 120 mg (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-coq10", "b": "Supports cellular energy and the heart. Especially helpful if you take a statin. When: Morning, with a meal that has fat. CoQ10 is fat-soluble. Take it with fat for absorption. Morning or midday. It can be energizing.", "k": "supplement Heart & Joints"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Copper (Glycinate) (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-copper", "b": "A trace mineral for energy, iron use, red blood cells, connective tissue and hair and skin pigment. When: With a meal. If you also take iron, take them on alternating days. They compete for absorption. Only take copper if your labs show you need it.", "k": "supplement Minerals & Blood"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Optiferin-C (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-optiferin-c", "b": "Gentle chelated iron with vitamin C to rebuild iron stores (ferritin) and support energy. When: With a meal, away from coffee, tea, calcium and magnesium. Coffee, tea, calcium and magnesium block iron. Space them 2 hours apart. Alternate days with copper if you take both. Dark stools are normal on iron.", "k": "supplement Minerals & Blood"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Trace Minerals (Thorne)", "u": "supplements.html#s-trace-minerals", "b": "Well-absorbed trace minerals (zinc, selenium, manganese, chromium, boron) for enzymes, hormones, thyroid and immunity. When: With lunch or another meal. Take with food. Zinc on an empty stomach can cause nausea. Pairs well with your lunch supplements.", "k": "supplement Minerals & Blood"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "UltraFlora Spectrum Probiotic (Metagenics)", "u": "supplements.html#s-ultraflora-spectrum", "b": "A 7-strain probiotic (30 billion CFU) for the upper and lower gut and immune health. When: Once daily, with a meal. Best kept refrigerated. On antibiotics? Take it 2 to 3 hours before or after your antibiotic. Pause probiotics 3 to 5 days before a gut test.", "k": "supplement Gut & Digestion"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Digestive Enzymes Ultra (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-digestive-enzymes-ultra", "b": "A broad blend of plant-based enzymes to help break down protein, fat, carbs, fiber and dairy sugar. When: At the start of a meal. Take with your first bites. Enzymes only work when food is there. Most helpful with your heaviest meals.", "k": "supplement Gut & Digestion"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "HistaEze (Designs for Health)", "u": "supplements.html#s-histaeze", "b": "Supports a healthy histamine response with quercetin, nettle, bromelain, luteolin, vitamin C and bicarbonate salts. When: With food, split morning and evening. Splitting the dose gives steadier support through the day.", "k": "supplement Immune & Brain"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Lion's Mane Extract (Host Defense)", "u": "supplements.html#s-lions-mane", "b": "A mushroom extract for focus, memory, mood and nervous system support. When: Morning or early afternoon. Take it straight or mix into water, tea, coffee or a smoothie. Consistency matters. Give it a few weeks.", "k": "supplement Immune & Brain"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "MycoShield Licorice Root Spray (Host Defense)", "u": "supplements.html#s-mycoshield-licorice", "b": "A travel-size immune spray with five mushroom extracts (agarikon, reishi, chaga, birch polypore, turkey tail) and licorice flavor. When: As needed, especially during travel, crowds or cold season. Keep it in your bag for travel and busy seasons.", "k": "supplement Immune & Brain"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Peri Meno Transition Support (Host Defense)", "u": "supplements.html#s-peri-meno", "b": "Mushrooms and herbs for the menopause transition: hot flashes, night sweats, energy and mood. When: Daily, with food or on an empty stomach. Give herbal hormone support 6 to 8 weeks to show its full effect. Track hot flashes and sleep in Heads Up.", "k": "supplement Hormones & Women's Health"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Libido Stim-F (Designs for Health)", "u": "supplements.html#s-libido-stim-f", "b": "Herbs and nutrients to support female desire, blood flow and healthy testosterone and estrogen metabolism. When: Morning, with breakfast. Morning is best. Ginseng and DHEA can be energizing.", "k": "supplement Hormones & Women's Health"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Saffro-Calm Plus (Patient One MediNutritionals)", "u": "supplements.html#s-saffro-calm", "b": "An oral spray with clinically studied saffron (affron) for mood and calm, plus echinacea. When: Morning and evening. About 12 hours apart for steady support.", "k": "supplement Mood, Stress & Sleep"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Herbal Zen (Wise Woman Herbals)", "u": "supplements.html#s-herbal-zen", "b": "An alcohol-free calming herbal blend for occasional stress and winding down. When: Evening, or during a stressful moment. Add to a little water or warm tea. Pairs well with your wind-down routine.", "k": "supplement Mood, Stress & Sleep"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "RelaxMax Cherry (GABA) (XYMOGEN)", "u": "supplements.html#s-relaxmax-cherry", "b": "A cherry drink mix with magnesium, inositol, taurine, GABA and L-theanine for calm and relaxation. When: Evening, or when you need to unwind. A calming swap for a nightcap. Sip it as part of your wind-down routine.", "k": "supplement Mood, Stress & Sleep"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "MSM Capsules (Pure Encapsulations)", "u": "supplements.html#s-msm", "b": "Organic sulfur (OptiMSM) for joints, connective tissue, skin, hair and nails. When: With meals. Spread doses across meals. Drink plenty of water.", "k": "supplement Heart & Joints"}, {"p": "Supplement", "t": "Grass-Fed Liver (Ancient Nutrition)", "u": "supplements.html#s-grass-fed-liver", "b": "Freeze-dried grass-fed liver: a whole-food source of iron, B12, vitamin A and other nutrients. When: With a meal. A food-based option when your labs show low iron or B12.", "k": "supplement Minerals & Blood"}];
